471
00:34:24.280 --> 00:34:27.680
♪ Tharangini Tharangini ♪
♪ Tharana- tharangini ♪

472
00:34:38.760 --> 00:34:43.520
Sir, the gunshots were fired
from that apartment balcony.

473
00:34:45.440 --> 00:34:48.400
But there is such a huge structure
in front of the stage.

474
00:34:48.520 --> 00:34:50.640
The shots would have
hit the structure, right?

475
00:34:57.800 --> 00:34:59.120
<b>Based on the entry wound...</b>

476
00:34:59.120 --> 00:35:03.040
you guessed that the bullet that hit the CM
was fired from
an angle of 118 to 120 degrees.

477
00:35:03.120 --> 00:35:04.160
<b>That's okay...</b>

478
00:35:04.280 --> 00:35:08.280
but it's not possible to shoot from that angle
from the
building you mentioned.

479
00:35:09.240 --> 00:35:12.680
They couldn't have even seen
the CM from that building.

480
00:35:16.440 --> 00:35:18.800
<b>So, what's your theory?</b>

481
00:35:19.400 --> 00:35:20.640
<b>Ricochet effect.</b>

482
00:35:21.280 --> 00:35:25.240
Listen... instead of a bullet,
imagine a fast approaching
car.

483
00:35:25.520 --> 00:35:26.440
<b>Okay?</b>

484
00:35:27.880 --> 00:35:30.440
<b>When it rams straight into a wall...</b>

485
00:35:31.040 --> 00:35:34.400
it ricochets, that is bounces off the wall,
and moves in the
 opposite direction.

486
00:35:35.760 --> 00:35:37.120
<b>But if the collision happens at an angle,</b>

487
00:35:37.160 --> 00:35:39.680
it moves in another direction
depending on the angle.

488
00:35:42.280 --> 00:35:47.000
Now imagine if the car hits a moving object,
like a train,
from an angle.

489
00:35:49.120 --> 00:35:50.640
<b>Due to the train's speed...</b>

490
00:35:50.640 --> 00:35:53.920
it will travel in some other angle
with several times the
original force.

491
00:35:55.400 --> 00:35:56.400
<b>Excuse me!</b>

492
00:35:56.520 --> 00:36:00.000
How did such a fast moving object
end up in this hall?

493
00:36:00.120 --> 00:36:01.520
<b>If I'm not wrong...</b>

494
00:36:01.560 --> 00:36:03.560
near the window through which
the bullet entered the
building...

495
00:36:03.640 --> 00:36:05.760
there must definitely be
a wall mounted fan.

496
00:36:06.120 --> 00:36:09.000
A fan that rotates at 400 rpm
in anti-clockwise direction.

497
00:36:10.760 --> 00:36:11.800
<b>Anand...</b>

498
00:36:14.120 --> 00:36:15.120
<b>Sir...</b>

499
00:36:39.760 --> 00:36:45.640
The assassin must have been seated 4th or 5th
in the 2nd row
 of the balcony...

500
00:36:45.640 --> 00:36:48.640
to get this 118 to 120 degree
ricochet angle.

501
00:36:54.040 --> 00:36:55.640
<b>Chief!</b>

502
00:36:55.640 --> 00:36:56.880
<b>Buddy...</b>

503
00:37:01.400 --> 00:37:05.400
He waited for the right time,
and remotely fired the gun
which was outside.

504
00:37:05.880 --> 00:37:09.880
He must have blind-sided everyone
by triggering it from
inside the hall.

505
00:37:30.800 --> 00:37:33.520
<b>Judy is the university topper in mathematics.</b>

506
00:37:33.760 --> 00:37:37.560
She left her home and her parents
to focus on maths and
research.

507
00:37:37.760 --> 00:37:41.880
She chose criminology as her main elective
in her final
semester.

508
00:37:42.280 --> 00:37:43.880
<b>She got obsessed with this case.</b>

509
00:37:44.160 --> 00:37:47.560
She discovered that there was maths involved
in every single
 aspect of this case.

510
00:37:47.880 --> 00:37:49.880
And that's how she came up
with her thesis.

511
00:37:50.120 --> 00:37:51.040
<b>The Cobra.</b>

512
00:37:55.520 --> 00:37:58.040
<b>Wow, what a surprise!</b>

513
00:37:59.000 --> 00:38:00.880
<b>I knew you'd eventually come to me.</b>

514
00:38:00.920 --> 00:38:02.400
<b>But this was too fast.</b>

515
00:38:02.520 --> 00:38:04.120
<b>Anyway, welcome peeps.</b>

516
00:38:04.280 --> 00:38:05.520
<b>Hi, ma'am.</b>

517
00:38:05.800 --> 00:38:07.240
<b>So, CBI Uncle...</b>

518
00:38:07.400 --> 00:38:09.160
<b>do you believe me atleast now?</b>

519
00:38:10.040 --> 00:38:13.640
In this case, your theory
definitely makes sense.

520
00:38:13.640 --> 00:38:14.680
<b>Accepted.</b>

521
00:38:14.760 --> 00:38:19.120
But what's the connection between the assassinations
in
Scotland and France and this case?

522
00:38:19.240 --> 00:38:21.520
<b>So far, maths is the only connection.</b>

523
00:38:22.040 --> 00:38:24.520
<b>He used the blind spot in France to escape.</b>

524
00:38:24.560 --> 00:38:27.520
He increased the sound to 120 decibels
at the church
wedding...

525
00:38:27.640 --> 00:38:30.680
and used the vibrations
to blast the crystal bulb.

526
00:38:30.920 --> 00:38:34.920
He calculated that the liquid nitrogen in it
would drip onto
 the steel chain and corrode it...

527
00:38:35.000 --> 00:38:38.240
and that the chain would be unable
to bear the 3.5 tonne
load and eventually snap.

528
00:38:38.400 --> 00:38:41.120
And the calculation that when it falls
from a height of 25
feet...

529
00:38:41.240 --> 00:38:46.400
it will fall with a force of 300 Pascals
and split the
ground open!

530
00:38:46.400 --> 00:38:49.640
Maths was the only common factor
in each and every single
move.

531
00:38:51.120 --> 00:38:53.520
<b>Then how did he find the tunnel and escape?</b>

532
00:38:54.160 --> 00:38:57.040
Aslan, that church was built
in the 16th century.

533
00:38:57.400 --> 00:39:01.120
Back in those days in Scotland,
to help the refugees
escape...

534
00:39:01.160 --> 00:39:04.040
there were several secret
tunnels built under churches.

535
00:39:04.120 --> 00:39:05.280
<b>That is known history.</b>

536
00:39:06.400 --> 00:39:08.240
<b>And his escape was very simple.</b>

537
00:39:08.280 --> 00:39:11.760
He used an ancient wartime strategy
like A Star algorithm...

538
00:39:11.880 --> 00:39:14.640
found the shortest exit route
from the church...

539
00:39:14.640 --> 00:39:16.440
<b>and escaped in a flash!</b>

540
00:39:16.520 --> 00:39:18.760
<b>Sir, I don't understand anything.</b>

541
00:39:18.800 --> 00:39:21.040
Are you going to listen
to this little girl's story...

542
00:39:21.120 --> 00:39:24.040
and use her college notebook
to do your investigation?

543
00:39:24.400 --> 00:39:31.160
Anand, Interpol aren't idiots to come all this way
blindly
trusting some little girl's theory.

544
00:39:31.680 --> 00:39:34.120
<b>Sir, that wasn't what I meant.</b>

545
00:39:34.880 --> 00:39:38.760
In ML algorithm, there is a study called
cloud of line
distribution.

546
00:39:39.240 --> 00:39:42.240
It analyses the strokes
of a person's handwriting...

547
00:39:42.400 --> 00:39:46.400
and accurately predicts which part
of the world he is from.

548
00:39:47.400 --> 00:39:49.280
<b>The guy who killed the Prince in Scotland...</b>

549
00:39:49.400 --> 00:39:53.520
made an accurate forgery of the father's signature
at the
palace he was staying at.

550
00:39:53.680 --> 00:39:57.120
Upon analysing the signature,
we found out he wasn't
European.

551
00:39:57.560 --> 00:39:58.640
<b>He is an Asian.</b>

552
00:39:58.680 --> 00:40:00.000
<b>To be more precise...</b>

553
00:40:00.000 --> 00:40:02.800
we found of that the chances
of him being an Indian is very
high.

554
00:40:03.400 --> 00:40:05.760
<b>That's when I came across Judy's thesis.</b>

555
00:40:06.240 --> 00:40:09.760
And the Indian connection
got me curious.

556
00:40:10.120 --> 00:40:12.280
The signature we found
at Coimbatore yesterday...

557
00:40:12.640 --> 00:40:13.880
<b>was in Tamil.</b>

558
00:40:14.120 --> 00:40:17.440
When I analysed those strokes,
it got confirmed...

559
00:40:18.000 --> 00:40:19.160
<b>that he is an Indian.</b>

560
00:40:19.240 --> 00:40:20.400
<b>And a Tamilian.</b>

561
00:40:21.000 --> 00:40:22.800
<b>Wow, really?</b>

562
00:40:23.160 --> 00:40:25.640
<b>Why are you getting excited about this?</b>

563
00:40:25.680 --> 00:40:28.120
<b>Ma'am, he is a genius!</b>

564
00:40:28.520 --> 00:40:30.520
I'm proud that
he is one of us.

565
00:40:30.560 --> 00:40:31.880
<b>Oh, god!</b>

566
00:40:32.520 --> 00:40:34.640
Are you okay with
helping us in this case?

567
00:40:39.240 --> 00:40:41.040
Don't you dare play
too hard to get!

568
00:40:41.240 --> 00:40:42.400
<b>What do you expect, ma'am?</b>

569
00:40:42.440 --> 00:40:45.000
I've already told you
that maths is the common factor.

570
00:40:45.440 --> 00:40:49.880
There must be one other connecting factor
behind all these
people who died.

571
00:40:50.240 --> 00:40:51.880
<b>Either a common story.</b>

572
00:40:51.920 --> 00:40:53.560
<b>Or a common enemy.</b>

573
00:40:53.640 --> 00:40:55.000
<b>There must definitely be something.</b>

574
00:40:55.640 --> 00:40:57.680
Maybe if they find out
what that is...

575
00:40:57.880 --> 00:41:01.920
I can atleast do my bit
to help stop the next assassination.

576
00:41:02.240 --> 00:41:04.920
But be assured,
that's easier said than done.

577
00:41:06.400 --> 00:41:07.760
<b>He is a cobra.</b>

578
00:41:08.040 --> 00:41:10.640
The most intelligent among
all the snakes.

579
00:41:11.880 --> 00:41:15.640
He knows how to change his appearance
and shift from one
form to another.

580
00:41:15.880 --> 00:41:18.640
He also knows to patiently hide
and wait for his target...

581
00:41:18.680 --> 00:41:21.160
<b>and strike within the blink of an eye.</b>

582
00:41:23.240 --> 00:41:24.240
<b>Let's see.</b>

583
00:41:24.400 --> 00:41:25.560
<b>Let's play this game.</b>

584
00:41:50.760 --> 00:41:54.240
Tamil, I've proofed the Su-Do-Ku puzzle
and sent it across.
- Okay, sir.

585
00:41:54.240 --> 00:41:55.640
Get it printed.
- Sure, sir.

586
00:42:21.680 --> 00:42:24.760
I scored the top marks
in the mid term exams, sir.

587
00:42:29.440 --> 00:42:31.760
Hello, sir!
Haven't seen you in a while.

588
00:42:31.880 --> 00:42:33.280
<b>How are you?</b>

589
00:42:33.760 --> 00:42:35.000
<b>Thanks!</b>

590
00:42:35.760 --> 00:42:38.280
Wow, what a style!
Beautiful.

591
00:42:40.760 --> 00:42:42.040
<b>You must see this.</b>

592
00:42:42.120 --> 00:42:43.280
<b>I'm talking to you!</b>

593
00:42:43.400 --> 00:42:46.880
Why is your sister-in-law whistling
through her nose?

594
00:42:47.920 --> 00:42:50.440
The entire family is inside.
Be careful!

595
00:42:51.560 --> 00:42:53.760
<b>We are unable to show face in town.</b>

596
00:42:53.880 --> 00:42:56.160
How can you just leave and come here
to live with some
random guy?

597
00:42:56.280 --> 00:42:57.680
<b>Imagine what people would say!</b>

598
00:42:57.800 --> 00:42:59.640
<b>They'd say I am living with him!</b>

599
00:42:59.920 --> 00:43:01.680
What's your problem
with accepting him?

600
00:43:01.760 --> 00:43:04.240
No matter what happens,
I won't get you married to him.

601
00:43:12.760 --> 00:43:14.400
I need to use the computer.
- Hello, sir...

602
00:43:15.640 --> 00:43:17.640
That system is free.
Can you use that?

603
00:43:56.760 --> 00:44:00.040
Mathi asked you to top up
this number for 129 rupees.

604
00:44:00.120 --> 00:44:01.760
<b>Fine, I'll do it in the morning.</b>

605
00:44:17.560 --> 00:44:18.800
<b>Hello, sir?</b>

606
00:44:19.040 --> 00:44:20.640
<b>I just got the confirmation.</b>

607
00:44:21.640 --> 00:44:24.760
Send his payment to those
50 charitable trusts.

608
00:44:25.120 --> 00:44:26.880
Okay, sir.
Thank you.

609
00:44:29.920 --> 00:44:31.640
<b>What is your daughter even saying?</b>

610
00:44:31.680 --> 00:44:34.040
If she isn't interested in this marriage,
why did you invite
 us?

611
00:44:34.120 --> 00:44:35.760
Brother, please...
- No point talking anymore.

612
00:44:35.800 --> 00:44:37.560
<b>Meena Sister, please listen to me.</b>

613
00:44:37.640 --> 00:44:39.880
She is making up stuff
just to spite us.

614
00:44:39.920 --> 00:44:41.440
<b>None of what she says is true.</b>

615
00:44:41.520 --> 00:44:44.280
Why are you still talking?
Start fighting!

616
00:44:44.440 --> 00:44:46.240
<b>Get the hell out of here!</b>

617
00:44:46.240 --> 00:44:48.400
Let's leave.
- Be quiet!

618
00:44:48.400 --> 00:44:50.680
Brother, please wait...
- Go away, you devil.

619
00:44:50.800 --> 00:44:52.400
<b>What kind of family is this?</b>

620
00:44:52.920 --> 00:44:54.000
<b>Cheers!</b>

621
00:44:54.040 --> 00:44:55.000
<b>Yeah, baby!</b>

622
00:44:55.040 --> 00:44:58.520
<b>The big boy has run helter-skelter--</b>

623
00:44:58.520 --> 00:45:00.520
<b>Stop it, you brainless moron!</b>

624
00:45:01.400 --> 00:45:02.920
<b>What do you think of yourself?</b>

625
00:45:03.160 --> 00:45:05.880
How dare you humiliate all of us
for the sake of some random
 guy?

626
00:45:06.000 --> 00:45:08.040
<b>Is he more important to you than us?</b>

627
00:45:08.520 --> 00:45:09.560
<b>Who is he?</b>

628
00:45:09.640 --> 00:45:12.880
How can we get you married to him
without knowing about his
family and background?

629
00:45:13.440 --> 00:45:17.640
He is raising some random orphan boy,
calling him 'little
one'.

630
00:45:17.880 --> 00:45:21.520
He prays to the sketch of some random woman,
referring to
her as his mother.

631
00:45:21.640 --> 00:45:23.400
<b>He hasn't said a thing about his family.</b>

632
00:45:23.400 --> 00:45:25.520
How can we get you married
to such a man?

633
00:45:25.640 --> 00:45:28.160
Don't run your mouth.
- You shut up!

634
00:45:29.520 --> 00:45:32.240
If he was born into a good family
and raised by a good
mother...

635
00:45:32.280 --> 00:45:35.400
he wouldn't take an innocent girl home
and make her family
suffer.

636
00:45:35.440 --> 00:45:37.160
<b>Just ignore what she says.</b>

637
00:45:38.120 --> 00:45:39.880
No one born into a good family--
- Shut up!

638
00:45:40.000 --> 00:45:41.240
<b>That's your limit.</b>

639
00:45:41.560 --> 00:45:43.120
<b>Don't run your mouth unnecessarily.</b>

640
00:45:44.400 --> 00:45:47.120
If he wanted to,
he could have already married me...

641
00:45:47.280 --> 00:45:50.440
made me cut ties with all of you,
and live a happy married
life.

642
00:45:51.280 --> 00:45:55.160
Instead, he valued all of you and insisted
that we need your
 consent for the wedding.

643
00:45:55.680 --> 00:45:57.920
<b>And look at how you treated him in return!</b>

644
00:45:58.120 --> 00:45:59.640
<b>Get out of my sight.</b>

645
00:46:00.040 --> 00:46:01.440
<b>I don't need any of you.</b>

646
00:46:02.000 --> 00:46:04.120
He is the only person
I need in my life.

647
00:46:04.920 --> 00:46:05.920
<b>Get it?</b>

648
00:46:06.120 --> 00:46:07.760
<b>He is all I need.</b>

649
00:46:11.520 --> 00:46:12.760
<b>What's this, Bhavana?</b>

650
00:46:14.120 --> 00:46:15.120
<b>Mathi...</b>

651
00:46:15.560 --> 00:46:17.640
Mathi, please don't take
anything they said to heart.

652
00:46:17.760 --> 00:46:18.760
<b>Please!</b>

653
00:46:19.400 --> 00:46:21.040
<b>Let me apologise on their behalf.</b>

654
00:46:21.440 --> 00:46:22.880
<b>I am the one who should apologise.</b>

655
00:46:24.680 --> 00:46:27.040
I shouldn't have strung you along
when I knew this will
never happen.

656
00:46:27.160 --> 00:46:28.880
Why do you say
this won't happen?

657
00:46:29.240 --> 00:46:30.880
<b>Because they won't agree to it?</b>

658
00:46:31.000 --> 00:46:32.800
<b>Who are they to decide my life?</b>

659
00:46:33.040 --> 00:46:34.520
You like me,
and I like you.

660
00:46:34.520 --> 00:46:35.880
<b>I don't like you, Bhavana.</b>

661
00:46:36.040 --> 00:46:37.240
<b>What are you saying, Mathi?</b>

662
00:46:38.520 --> 00:46:42.280
<b>I respect you and the social work you do.</b>

663
00:46:43.120 --> 00:46:45.680
But that...
- Are you saying that isn't love?

664
00:46:48.040 --> 00:46:49.440
<b>You are lying, Mathi.</b>

665
00:46:49.680 --> 00:46:52.160
I know how your face changes
when you lie.

666
00:46:53.040 --> 00:46:56.560
I know what the smallest of movements
in your eyes mean.

667
00:46:57.880 --> 00:46:59.440
<b>What they said was wrong.</b>

668
00:46:59.680 --> 00:47:01.280
<b>Just tell me what I should do now.</b>

669
00:47:02.880 --> 00:47:03.920
<b>This won't happen.</b>

670
00:47:04.520 --> 00:47:06.000
<b>Listen to your family.</b>

671
00:47:07.400 --> 00:47:09.040
Leave this house.
- What are you saying?

672
00:47:09.120 --> 00:47:10.240
<b>I won't leave, Mathi.</b>

673
00:47:10.280 --> 00:47:12.520
Even if you say it a thousand times,
I won't leave.

674
00:47:12.560 --> 00:47:13.680
<b>I will continue to live here.</b>

675
00:47:13.760 --> 00:47:15.400
<b>I'd even give my life for you.</b>

676
00:47:15.440 --> 00:47:17.040
<b>Don't say that again and again, Bhavana!</b>

677
00:47:20.400 --> 00:47:22.240
I don't want anyone
to sacrifice their life for me.

678
00:47:23.640 --> 00:47:25.000
What should I say
to make you leave?

679
00:47:25.000 --> 00:47:27.240
<b>I told you several times not to stay here.</b>

680
00:47:27.440 --> 00:47:28.680
<b>But you never listened!</b>

681
00:47:31.760 --> 00:47:33.520
<b>I really don't like you.</b>

682
00:47:34.400 --> 00:47:35.560
<b>I don't want you.</b>

683
00:47:36.040 --> 00:47:38.280
<b>I don't want anyone else except you, Mathi.</b>

684
00:47:45.520 --> 00:47:47.520
Without you,
I don't know if I can...

685
00:47:49.240 --> 00:47:53.000
Will you atleast come to see me
when I die someday?

686
00:47:53.440 --> 00:47:55.560
Atleast on that day,
don't lie about not liking me...

687
00:47:55.640 --> 00:47:57.800
and whisper the truth
into my ears atleast once, Mathi.

688
00:48:01.160 --> 00:48:03.000
<b>I won't disturb you anymore.</b>

689
00:48:06.240 --> 00:48:07.640
<b>Bhavana...</b>

690
00:48:07.760 --> 00:48:09.680
Bhavana, please stop.
- Sister, please!

691
00:48:09.680 --> 00:48:10.920
<b>Bhavana, listen to me.</b>

692
00:48:13.640 --> 00:48:14.760
<b>Very good!</b>

693
00:48:14.920 --> 00:48:16.440
<b>You did really well there!</b>

694
00:48:17.000 --> 00:48:19.440
If this is your decision,
you could have said it four years
ago.

695
00:48:20.000 --> 00:48:22.760
<b>Give me one reason why you don't like her.</b>

696
00:48:24.680 --> 00:48:25.760
<b>Should I say it?</b>

697
00:48:26.760 --> 00:48:27.760
<b>Jennifer.</b>

698
00:48:33.000 --> 00:48:34.000
<b>I love you.</b>

699
00:48:36.560 --> 00:48:39.000
You are doing this because
you are still thinking about her.

700
00:48:43.520 --> 00:48:44.640
<b>This is wrong, Mathi.</b>

701
00:48:45.000 --> 00:48:46.240
<b>Very, very wrong.</b>

702
00:49:12.640 --> 00:49:13.760
<b>Yeah, next one?</b>

703
00:49:14.880 --> 00:49:15.880
<b>Hello, sir.</b>

704
00:49:15.920 --> 00:49:17.440
<b>What's the purpose of your trip?</b>

705
00:49:19.160 --> 00:49:20.680
<b>What's the purpose of your trip?</b>

706
00:49:22.920 --> 00:49:24.400
<b>Holiday.</b>

707
00:49:24.640 --> 00:49:26.120
<b>Oh, holiday?</b>

708
00:49:26.640 --> 00:49:27.800
<b>Enjoy your trip.</b>

709
00:49:28.880 --> 00:49:30.280
<b>I will.</b>

710
00:49:40.280 --> 00:49:42.640
Sir, someone has hacked into
all the servers to print these.

711
00:49:42.760 --> 00:49:45.240
Not just here,
but all the floors in this building.

712
00:49:53.440 --> 00:49:54.920
<b>This is going to be his next hit.</b>

713
00:49:55.160 --> 00:49:56.160
<b>How do you know?</b>

714
00:49:56.760 --> 00:49:58.120
<b>Has this happened before?</b>

715
00:49:58.160 --> 00:49:59.240
<b>Yes.</b>

716
00:49:59.800 --> 00:50:01.120
<b>It happened once previously.</b>

717
00:50:01.640 --> 00:50:02.800
<b>Same fashion.</b>

718
00:50:03.400 --> 00:50:05.800
They hacked the Interpol servers,
just like this.

719
00:50:06.120 --> 00:50:07.120
<b>But...</b>

720
00:50:07.760 --> 00:50:09.000
<b>who is doing this?</b>

721
00:50:09.240 --> 00:50:13.000
Either he is doing this himself
to increase the thrill
factor...

722
00:50:13.440 --> 00:50:17.520
or someone who wants him to get caught
is doing this.

723
00:50:18.000 --> 00:50:20.440
<b>But what does this mean?</b>

724
00:50:22.400 --> 00:50:23.880
<b>HKG</b>

725
00:50:24.800 --> 00:50:26.240
<b>I've seen this somewhere.</b>

726
00:50:26.880 --> 00:50:28.400
<b>James, is this Hong Kong?</b>

727
00:50:29.160 --> 00:50:30.640
Yes, Chief.
You are right.

728
00:50:31.240 --> 00:50:32.880
<b>HKG is Hong Kong.</b>

729
00:50:33.000 --> 00:50:34.120
<b>What about LED then?</b>

730
00:50:36.520 --> 00:50:38.240
<b>St. Petersburg, Russia.</b>

731
00:50:39.240 --> 00:50:42.520
He is travelling from Hong Kong
to St. Petersburg to do
something.

732
00:50:43.280 --> 00:50:45.000
<b>Alert the Russian Intelligence.</b>

733
00:50:45.000 --> 00:50:48.000
Make a list of all passengers who travelled
from Hong Kong
over the last week.

734
00:51:08.800 --> 00:51:10.560
<b>But these numbers...</b>

735
00:51:10.920 --> 00:51:12.440
<b>there is some clue in it.</b>

736
00:51:13.400 --> 00:51:14.440
<b>Don't worry, Aslan.</b>

737
00:51:14.760 --> 00:51:16.440
My mind's been at it
for a while now.

738
00:51:16.640 --> 00:51:18.760
Give me sometime.
I'll get this.

739
00:51:19.440 --> 00:51:25.040
James, I need details on all the important events
scheduled
to happen in St. Petersburg this week.

740
00:51:38.640 --> 00:51:39.520
<b>Hello?</b>

741
00:51:39.560 --> 00:51:40.640
<b>This is Nawab speaking.</b>

742
00:51:40.640 --> 00:51:42.920
The Interpol have tracked
your man all the way to Russia.

743
00:51:42.920 --> 00:51:44.760
What the hell have you done?
Idiots!

744
00:51:44.880 --> 00:51:46.280
<b>Come to the hotel immediately.</b>

745
00:51:48.760 --> 00:51:50.000
<b>Sir, we received your mail.</b>

746
00:51:50.280 --> 00:51:51.760
<b>In fact, due to security reasons...</b>

747
00:51:51.880 --> 00:51:55.120
we have cancelled all events 
in St. Petersburg for the next
 one week.

748
00:51:55.520 --> 00:51:57.240
<b>Because the president is visiting here.</b>

749
00:51:57.560 --> 00:51:58.760
<b>The president is visiting the city?</b>

750
00:51:59.160 --> 00:52:00.000
<b>When?</b>

751
00:52:00.040 --> 00:52:01.240
<b>Day after tomorrow.</b>

752
00:52:01.520 --> 00:52:04.680
The People's Front Party
are hosting a big event here.

753
00:52:04.880 --> 00:52:09.240
The Russian President, his cabinet ministers,
and several
other international delegates will be here...

754
00:52:09.400 --> 00:52:11.520
<b>to meet the party's supporters.</b>

755
00:52:12.240 --> 00:52:13.120
<b>Fish!</b>

756
00:52:15.240 --> 00:52:17.280
Nellai, how did this information
get leaked?

757
00:52:17.400 --> 00:52:20.160
I'm wondering too.
Maybe it got leaked from your side...

758
00:52:20.240 --> 00:52:22.560
There is no chance
of an information leak from my side.

759
00:52:22.640 --> 00:52:23.920
<b>Tell him to come back.</b>

760
00:52:24.040 --> 00:52:25.240
<b>Your guy is going to get caught.</b>

761
00:52:25.240 --> 00:52:27.120
<b>If Rishi's name comes out...</b>

762
00:52:27.640 --> 00:52:29.120
<b>all of us will be in danger.</b>

763
00:52:29.640 --> 00:52:31.240
<b>This isn't some game, Nellaiappan.</b>

764
00:52:31.520 --> 00:52:32.800
<b>Come back?</b>

765
00:52:34.240 --> 00:52:38.640
Once he gets started on a mission,
I can't even reach him.

766
00:52:38.680 --> 00:52:41.640
Everything will go as per plan.
Don't worry.

767
00:52:43.520 --> 00:52:44.680
<b>Yes, Officer Aslan?</b>

768
00:52:44.760 --> 00:52:46.240
<b>I heard about the purpose of your visit.</b>

769
00:52:46.240 --> 00:52:47.680
<b>So, what are you saying?</b>

770
00:52:48.000 --> 00:52:50.240
<b>General, we have to stop this event.</b>

771
00:52:50.400 --> 00:52:53.120
Because some important person
could get killed in it.

772
00:52:53.280 --> 00:52:55.920
<b>Who do you think that could be?</b>

773
00:52:56.120 --> 00:52:58.400
I don't know.
It could even be the president.

774
00:53:00.640 --> 00:53:01.800
<b>Listen, officer...</b>

775
00:53:02.120 --> 00:53:03.680
<b>I understand your concerns.</b>

776
00:53:03.880 --> 00:53:07.640
But this event is a matter of
honour and prestige for our
country.

777
00:53:08.160 --> 00:53:10.000
<b>We can't cancel it under any circumstances.</b>

778
00:53:10.280 --> 00:53:14.760
You believe some random hacker who says
the Russian
President will be killed on Russian soil?

779
00:53:14.760 --> 00:53:16.440
<b>It is so laughable.</b>

780
00:53:17.000 --> 00:53:18.680
<b>This is Russia, officer.</b>

781
00:53:18.800 --> 00:53:23.240
Our defence and security is
much more powerful than you can
imagine.

782
00:53:26.560 --> 00:53:27.680
<b>What's going on?</b>

783
00:53:28.120 --> 00:53:30.240
General, you've got to come out
and see this.

784
00:53:30.400 --> 00:53:32.800
<b>Someone has hacked our entire defence tower.</b>

785
00:53:45.040 --> 00:53:46.400
<b>Lazy fellows!</b>

786
00:53:46.560 --> 00:53:48.920
How long does it take for you
to come out?

787
00:53:49.400 --> 00:53:50.640
<b>Tell them to shut the tower down.</b>

788
00:53:50.680 --> 00:53:52.440
Hey, Aslan!
- Shut the tower down immediately.

789
00:53:52.440 --> 00:53:54.400
<b>This is a small gift from me.</b>

790
00:53:54.400 --> 00:53:56.240
<b>For you, my friend.</b>

791
00:53:56.920 --> 00:53:58.120
<b>Okay?</b>

792
00:53:58.240 --> 00:53:59.680
<b>Here you go.</b>

793
00:54:02.520 --> 00:54:04.760
Your guy is going to get caught.
Tell him to come back.

794
00:54:05.120 --> 00:54:07.040
<b>If Rishi's name comes out...</b>

795
00:54:07.120 --> 00:54:09.760
Listen carefully.
- All of us will be in danger.

796
00:54:11.400 --> 00:54:13.520
Your guy is going to get caught.
Tell him to come back.

797
00:54:14.120 --> 00:54:16.400
<b>If Rishi's name comes out...</b>

798
00:54:16.520 --> 00:54:19.520
<b>Rishi... Rishi... Rishi... Rishi...</b>

799
00:54:20.520 --> 00:54:22.640
Some guy is giving us
all this information...

800
00:54:23.000 --> 00:54:26.000
but why isn't he revealing
the identity of the assassin?

801
00:54:26.440 --> 00:54:32.880
Maybe he doesn't know how or
under what guise the assassin
would come.

802
00:54:33.440 --> 00:54:36.240
What if he is just sharing
whatever information he has with
us...

803
00:54:36.280 --> 00:54:38.000
because he wants to
get the assassin caught?

804
00:54:38.040 --> 00:54:39.920
<b>Rishi, Rishi, Rishi...</b>

805
00:54:40.000 --> 00:54:42.000
<b>Listen, listen...</b>

806
00:54:42.000 --> 00:54:43.880
Listen, listen, listen,
listen, listen, listen!

807
00:54:44.520 --> 00:54:47.120
<b>Rajiv Rishi of Rishi Corporations.</b>

808
00:54:47.640 --> 00:54:49.440
<b>He is the connecting factor.</b>

809
00:54:50.880 --> 00:54:54.680
Orissa's CM, the Prince of Scotland,
the Mayor in France...

810
00:54:54.880 --> 00:55:00.000
all of them opposed Rishi
and Rishi Corp one way or the
other.

811
00:55:01.400 --> 00:55:04.120
<b>So, who could his target in Russia be?</b>

812
00:55:05.240 --> 00:55:07.560
<b>It could be Dimitri Yugoslav.</b>

813
00:55:07.880 --> 00:55:09.240
<b>He is an important leader.</b>

814
00:55:09.760 --> 00:55:11.120
<b>Our country's Defence Minister.</b>

815
00:55:11.160 --> 00:55:12.920
<b>Yes, it is the Defence Minister.</b>

816
00:55:13.280 --> 00:55:14.280
<b>How do you know?</b>

817
00:55:14.400 --> 00:55:15.560
<b>It is simple maths.</b>

818
00:55:15.680 --> 00:55:17.800
<b>4136P66</b>

819
00:55:18.000 --> 00:55:21.120
P is for point.
So, 4136.66

820
00:55:21.520 --> 00:55:25.120
<b>The square is 17111955.</b>

821
00:55:26.520 --> 00:55:28.920
<b>17-11-1955</b>

822
00:55:29.240 --> 00:55:30.800
<b>Defence Minister's birthday.</b>

823
00:55:30.920 --> 00:55:35.120
Defence Minister Dimitri is involved
in an arms racket with
Rishi Corp.

824
00:55:35.560 --> 00:55:41.440
The Defence Minister shut down
Rishi Corp's operations in
Russia to save himself.

825
00:55:41.520 --> 00:55:42.760
<b>This has to be him.</b>

826
00:55:42.880 --> 00:55:44.880
<b>Officer Aslan, what do we do now?</b>

827
00:55:44.920 --> 00:55:47.400
We can't cancel this event
at any cost.

828
00:55:47.400 --> 00:55:49.880
At the same time, we have to
stop this assassination too.

829
00:55:49.920 --> 00:55:51.760
<b>The assassin will be stopped, General.</b>

830
00:55:52.120 --> 00:55:54.120
I won't let him
take one step forward!

831
00:56:03.040 --> 00:56:05.440
No matter what calculations
your genius comes up with...

832
00:56:06.000 --> 00:56:07.680
<b>He only plays with numbers.</b>

833
00:56:08.640 --> 00:56:11.000
I will give him more numbers
to play with this time.

834
00:56:11.680 --> 00:56:13.240
<b>Good morning, St. Petersburg.</b>

835
00:56:13.280 --> 00:56:15.760
<b>We are outside the Presidential Palace.</b>

836
00:56:15.880 --> 00:56:20.120
Thousands of supporters of the People's Party
have gathered
here.

837
00:56:20.120 --> 00:56:25.880
The President will be leaving shortly
for the event with his
 top ministers.

838
00:56:31.760 --> 00:56:33.880
Nikolai, what are you gawking at?
Hurry up!

839
00:56:34.040 --> 00:56:35.640
Right away!
- Flash news...

840
00:56:35.680 --> 00:56:37.000
<b>Roll it!</b>

841
00:56:38.640 --> 00:56:39.440
<b>Rolling...</b>

842
00:56:39.520 --> 00:56:43.040
The Defence Ministry has made
an important announcement just
 now.

843
00:56:43.120 --> 00:56:49.760
According to it, the venue of the event
has been shifted due
 to security concerns.

844
00:56:49.920 --> 00:56:53.560
We've received information that the event
will now happen at
 Paul Fortress.

845
00:56:53.760 --> 00:56:59.800
The Defence Ministry has requested all party members
and
supporters to gather at Paul Fortress.

846
00:57:00.120 --> 00:57:01.240
<b>Okay?</b>

847
00:57:01.400 --> 00:57:02.520
<b>Okay, good.</b>

848
00:57:03.000 --> 00:57:04.880
<b>Could they have received any information?</b>

849
00:57:12.560 --> 00:57:13.640
<b>Who is that guy?</b>

850
00:57:24.640 --> 00:57:25.680
<b>Hang on.</b>

851
00:57:28.240 --> 00:57:29.400
<b>Paul Fortress.</b>

852
00:57:29.680 --> 00:57:31.760
It's on a tiny island
on Neva river.

853
00:57:31.920 --> 00:57:33.520
There is only one way
to get there.

854
00:57:33.520 --> 00:57:36.040
I'm sure they must have locked
and secured the entire area.

855
00:57:38.520 --> 00:57:40.400
What do you say?
Are we doing it?

856
00:57:41.280 --> 00:57:42.760
<b>Genius, are we doing it?</b>

857
00:58:59.880 --> 00:59:01.120
<b>Body double.</b>

858
00:59:16.120 --> 00:59:19.640
They've played us with a body double
while the real defence
minister was here all along.

859
00:59:33.000 --> 00:59:34.000
<b>Alright, get ready.</b>

860
00:59:36.240 --> 00:59:37.880
<b>So this will be our eyes.</b>

861
00:59:38.000 --> 00:59:39.640
<b>You sure we don't have any blind spots?</b>

862
00:59:39.640 --> 00:59:40.560
<b>No, sir.</b>

863
00:59:40.640 --> 00:59:43.400
We have covered the venue
from all sides.

864
00:59:43.520 --> 00:59:45.240
All cameras...
are you guys ready?

865
00:59:45.520 --> 00:59:47.120
<b>This game is about to end.</b>

866
00:59:47.880 --> 00:59:49.520
<b>Snipers, take positions.</b>

867
00:59:55.440 --> 00:59:56.400
<b>Alpha, ready.</b>

868
00:59:56.520 --> 00:59:57.440
<b>Delta, ready.</b>

869
01:00:04.880 --> 01:00:07.240
Seize the place.
Close all the exits.

870
01:00:10.160 --> 01:00:11.240
<b>It's locked.</b>

871
01:00:13.440 --> 01:00:14.440
<b>Scanners...</b>

872
01:00:25.240 --> 01:00:26.560
<b>This was a trap for us.</b>

873
01:00:26.640 --> 01:00:28.880
Our fingerprints won't match
with the ones on the biometric
scanner.

874
01:00:29.000 --> 01:00:31.240
We will get caught for sure.
There is no way we can escape.

875
01:00:31.400 --> 01:00:32.640
<b>What are we going to do now?</b>

876
01:00:38.640 --> 01:00:40.520
<b>It's very hard.</b>

877
01:00:40.640 --> 01:00:41.920
<b>Get the hell out of here.</b>

878
01:00:42.160 --> 01:00:43.520
<b>No chance!</b>

879
01:00:43.640 --> 01:00:45.440
<b>We must do something immediately.</b>

880
01:00:45.520 --> 01:00:46.760
<b>We are locked.</b>

881
01:00:48.120 --> 01:00:50.400
<b>See, looks like you are scared!</b>

882
01:00:50.560 --> 01:00:52.560
You can't do it, can you?
- But you can!

883
01:00:53.680 --> 01:00:55.120
<b>Only you can do it!</b>

884
01:00:55.760 --> 01:00:56.640
<b>Think!</b>

885
01:00:56.760 --> 01:00:57.560
<b>Think!</b>

886
01:00:57.640 --> 01:00:58.760
<b>Think hard!</b>

887
01:01:08.400 --> 01:01:09.520
<b>Don't do it!</b>

888
01:01:12.400 --> 01:01:13.440
<b>Escape!</b>

889
01:01:41.640 --> 01:01:43.880
<b>Please listen to me.</b>

890
01:01:50.920 --> 01:01:52.680
<b>You will listen to me, won't you?</b>

891
01:01:56.520 --> 01:01:57.560
<b>Listen to me!</b>

892
01:01:57.640 --> 01:01:59.400
Don't do this.
Get out of here.

893
01:02:15.000 --> 01:02:16.400
<b>Hold on!</b>

894
01:02:16.640 --> 01:02:18.800
<b>Where do you think you are going?</b>

895
01:02:20.240 --> 01:02:22.800
Looks like someone finally beat you 
at numbers and boxed
you in!

896
01:02:22.880 --> 01:02:24.440
<b>You are a dead man today.</b>

897
01:02:28.400 --> 01:02:30.880
We are losing time, genius.
We are losing time!

898
01:02:30.880 --> 01:02:32.760
Stay focused.
Your mind shouldn't be here.

899
01:02:32.880 --> 01:02:34.240
<b>Your mind shouldn't be here.</b>

900
01:02:34.240 --> 01:02:36.000
<b>Notice every little detail.</b>

901
01:02:36.040 --> 01:02:37.520
<b>You will surely find a loophole.</b>

902
01:02:37.520 --> 01:02:38.640
<b>Go there!</b>

903
01:02:41.880 --> 01:02:43.880
The security team is in
an arrowhead formation.

904
01:02:43.880 --> 01:02:47.240
They will secure the minister
in exactly 1.45 seconds
reaction time.

905
01:03:27.240 --> 01:03:28.640
<b>Everyone is saying different things--</b>

906
01:03:30.120 --> 01:03:31.400
<b>He has found something!</b>

907
01:03:36.000 --> 01:03:37.000
<b>Disturbance!</b>

908
01:03:37.040 --> 01:03:40.240
<b>Ma, something smells really bad here.</b>

909
01:03:40.280 --> 01:03:42.240
<b>Let's leave, Ma.</b>

910
01:03:45.800 --> 01:03:49.000
<b>Ma, something smells really bad here.</b>

911
01:03:49.120 --> 01:03:50.920
<b>Let's leave, Ma.</b>

912
01:03:53.040 --> 01:03:54.520
<b>It's methane gas.</b>

913
01:03:55.440 --> 01:03:57.520
The manholes in a sewer channel
are generally connected.

914
01:03:57.560 --> 01:04:00.520
And yes, the next manhole
is right next to the stage.

915
01:04:00.800 --> 01:04:03.400
We just need to set off
a small spark in this manhole.

916
01:04:04.040 --> 01:04:05.880
<b>We can blow up the entire stage.</b>

917
01:04:06.640 --> 01:04:07.680
<b>He's got it!</b>

918
01:04:07.760 --> 01:04:09.880
He's got an idea!
He's done it!

919
01:04:42.240 --> 01:04:43.160
<b>Boom!</b>

920
01:04:59.000 --> 01:05:01.400
Camera crew...
is anyone on the line?

921
01:05:01.400 --> 01:05:03.800
Is anyone connected? Please reply.
- Have we lost all the
visuals?

922
01:05:03.880 --> 01:05:06.000
Not even one is active?
- Sir, I think everyone is injured.

923
01:05:06.000 --> 01:05:07.920
We aren't receiving visuals
from any of them.

924
01:05:12.880 --> 01:05:15.240
Sir, we are receiving visuals
from camera 7.

925
01:05:15.800 --> 01:05:18.040
<b>Camera 7, can you hear me?</b>

926
01:05:18.160 --> 01:05:20.560
I need a visual of the minister.
Do you copy?

927
01:05:20.680 --> 01:05:22.640
Do you copy?
- Copy that.

928
01:05:22.680 --> 01:05:24.400
Sir, he can hear us.
- Good.

929
01:05:24.400 --> 01:05:26.120
<b>Ask camera 7 to keep moving forward.</b>

930
01:05:26.120 --> 01:05:28.400
And get me the visual on
the giant screen. - Yes, sir.

931
01:05:28.680 --> 01:05:31.000
<b>Camera 7, go inside the tunnel.</b>

932
01:05:31.160 --> 01:05:33.040
<b>Get closer to the minister.</b>

933
01:05:58.680 --> 01:06:01.760
I hadn't planned such a
painful death for you.

934
01:06:03.240 --> 01:06:04.400
<b>Sorry.</b>

935
01:06:30.560 --> 01:06:31.880
<b>Call the paramedics!</b>

936
01:06:32.000 --> 01:06:33.280
<b>It's an emergency.</b>

937
01:06:46.000 --> 01:06:47.280
<b>Where could he escape from here?</b>

938
01:06:47.400 --> 01:06:49.520
Sir, he can't escape anywhere
from this river.

939
01:06:49.640 --> 01:06:52.400
The water is so cold, no one can
survive for more than 2
minutes.

940
01:06:52.760 --> 01:06:54.120
<b>He will surely get caught.</b>

941
01:07:03.240 --> 01:07:05.520
Sir, he isn't the actual press reporter
from RT.

942
01:07:06.000 --> 01:07:07.000
<b>Oh, damn!</b>

943
01:07:11.240 --> 01:07:14.000
Officer, we've circulated
his photo everywhere.

944
01:07:14.240 --> 01:07:16.280
We've informed all the airports
and sea ports.

945
01:07:16.440 --> 01:07:17.800
<b>There is no way he can escape.</b>

946
01:07:33.520 --> 01:07:36.000
Here are your reports.
Consult the doctor. - Okay, miss.

947
01:07:36.120 --> 01:07:37.920
Whatever it is,
make it quick.

948
01:07:38.400 --> 01:07:39.640
<b>Because I need to go home.</b>

949
01:07:39.640 --> 01:07:41.000
<b>I have a family of my own.</b>

950
01:07:41.440 --> 01:07:44.280
I can't live a solitary life
by shunning everyone around me.

951
01:07:44.560 --> 01:07:46.560
Kumaresan, if you want to go home,
just go already.

952
01:07:46.640 --> 01:07:47.800
<b>Don't annoy me.</b>

953
01:07:47.920 --> 01:07:49.440
<b>Why are you getting annoyed?</b>

954
01:07:49.640 --> 01:07:52.000
We are the ones who should
be annoyed by what you do!

955
01:07:52.240 --> 01:07:54.800
A girl trusted you and came home
but you chased her away.

956
01:07:54.920 --> 01:07:56.520
Where did she go?
Is she alive or dead?

957
01:07:56.560 --> 01:07:57.880
<b>You don't care, do you?</b>

958
01:07:58.160 --> 01:08:01.160
Not just you, none of us
can see Bhavana again.

959
01:08:03.520 --> 01:08:06.160
In Sudan, they have a reform school
in the desert...

960
01:08:06.240 --> 01:08:09.920
for children who get involved in
guns, drugs, and terrorism.

961
01:08:10.000 --> 01:08:12.240
She's signed an agreement to serve
there for 15 years.

962
01:08:12.240 --> 01:08:13.520
<b>She is going to leave.</b>

963
01:08:14.920 --> 01:08:16.240
<b>Her flight is tomorrow.</b>

964
01:08:19.000 --> 01:08:20.520
<b>Mr. Mathiyazhagan...</b>

965
01:08:22.280 --> 01:08:25.520
<b>Seizures, hyperthermia.</b>

966
01:08:25.640 --> 01:08:31.440
Did you go to any cold places
in the recent past?

967
01:08:31.640 --> 01:08:32.640
<b>Yes, doctor.</b>

968
01:08:32.640 --> 01:08:35.640
He'd gone to Valparai to teach children,
and got back only
this morning.

969
01:08:35.880 --> 01:08:39.440
He's been complaining of bad chills
and head aches since he
got back.

970
01:08:39.920 --> 01:08:41.520
<b>Seriously, Mr. Mathi?</b>

971
01:08:42.560 --> 01:08:46.000
Does it get that cold
in Valparai these days?

972
01:08:46.560 --> 01:08:48.800
<b>Mathi, he is talking to you!</b>

973
01:08:49.240 --> 01:08:51.560
<b>Enlargement of ventricles.</b>

974
01:08:52.240 --> 01:08:54.520
<b>The cortical volume has reduced.</b>

975
01:09:01.640 --> 01:09:07.240
Is there anything unusual about
Mathi's behaviour in recent
times?

976
01:09:07.680 --> 01:09:09.400
No, doctor.
No such thing.

977
01:09:12.400 --> 01:09:17.040
Mathi, do you have any prior history
of mental illness?

978
01:09:17.520 --> 01:09:20.520
Has anyone diagnosed you
for schizophrenia?

979
01:09:20.760 --> 01:09:23.120
<b>Or disorders like schizoid?</b>

980
01:09:23.440 --> 01:09:24.560
<b>I won't leave, Mathi.</b>

981
01:09:24.640 --> 01:09:26.880
Even if you say it a thousand times,
I won't leave.

982
01:09:27.120 --> 01:09:28.400
<b>I will continue to live here.</b>

983
01:09:28.440 --> 01:09:29.520
<b>Mathi...</b>

984
01:09:30.240 --> 01:09:31.880
<b>Do you hear me?</b>

985
01:09:32.000 --> 01:09:34.520
See, I just want you to
be there for me.

986
01:09:34.760 --> 01:09:37.280
I can see you are really confused
about something.

987
01:09:37.520 --> 01:09:39.680
<b>I don't need anyone else except you, Mathi.</b>

988
01:09:39.760 --> 01:09:43.440
I can do something only if you
tell me what that is.

989
01:09:43.560 --> 01:09:45.240
<b>Is there something else in your mind?</b>

990
01:09:45.280 --> 01:09:47.280
I will know what it is
only if you tell me.

991
01:09:47.400 --> 01:09:51.760
Have you had extreme depression
or anxiety attacks in the
past?

992
01:09:52.240 --> 01:09:53.640
<b>Can you tell me about your past?</b>

993
01:09:53.680 --> 01:09:55.880
You are doing this because
of something from your past!

994
01:09:55.880 --> 01:09:57.520
<b>To help you get over me...</b>

995
01:09:57.520 --> 01:10:02.040
an angel will come to shower you
with love and attention.

996
01:10:02.160 --> 01:10:03.400
<b>I love you.</b>

997
01:10:09.000 --> 01:10:10.040
<b>Mathi...</b>

998
01:10:11.000 --> 01:10:12.520
<b>Do you hallucinate?</b>

999
01:10:14.560 --> 01:10:18.120
<b>Do you hear things that no one else does?</b>

1000
01:10:18.160 --> 01:10:23.680
<b>Or see things no one else does?</b>

1001
01:10:24.120 --> 01:10:25.880
<b>Do you hallucinate?</b>

1002
01:10:31.920 --> 01:10:33.520
<b>He's got some plan!</b>

1003
01:10:33.520 --> 01:10:34.440
<b>I'll take care of it.</b>

1004
01:10:34.520 --> 01:10:36.400
Sure, go ahead.
Good night!

1005
01:10:36.880 --> 01:10:37.880
<b>Don't do it.</b>

1006
01:10:41.560 --> 01:10:42.640
<b>You sure?</b>

1007
01:10:46.800 --> 01:10:48.000
<b>Good, then.</b>

1008
01:10:48.800 --> 01:10:50.120
<b>What happened, doctor?</b>

1009
01:10:50.400 --> 01:10:54.440
You mentioned hallucinations etc.
Is it something serious?

1010
01:10:54.920 --> 01:10:59.800
See, there are two categories
of people who hallucinate.

1011
01:11:00.040 --> 01:11:06.000
The first category can't tell apart
what is real and what is
 not...

1012
01:11:06.280 --> 01:11:09.640
so they get mentally affected
and become very serious.

1013
01:11:09.880 --> 01:11:14.880
But the other category can tell apart
what is real and what
is not.

1014
01:11:15.040 --> 01:11:19.520
They are smart enough to accept it
and learn to live with
it.

1015
01:11:19.760 --> 01:11:21.760
<b>They might appear very normal too.</b>

1016
01:11:22.440 --> 01:11:25.640
I had to ask because I suspected
that could be the case with
 him.

1017
01:11:26.240 --> 01:11:27.520
<b>Your guy is going to get caught.</b>

1018
01:11:27.560 --> 01:11:28.880
<b>Tell him to come back.</b>

1019
01:11:29.120 --> 01:11:31.000
<b>If Rishi's name comes out...</b>

1020
01:11:31.240 --> 01:11:33.920
Officer, before you start accusing
our Capo...

1021
01:11:34.040 --> 01:11:37.120
I'm sure your forensic analyst team
verified Nawab's video.

1022
01:11:37.160 --> 01:11:39.880
Can you tell me the
date and time stamp on it?

1023
01:11:40.040 --> 01:11:43.040
It was three days ago.
At 10 pm IST.

1024
01:11:43.240 --> 01:11:45.520
Perfect! These are
Nawab's termination papers.

1025
01:11:45.920 --> 01:11:48.920
<b>We fired him exactly 74 days ago.</b>

1026
01:11:49.000 --> 01:11:53.000
There is no connection between Nawab
and our Capo or Rishi
Corporations.

1027
01:11:53.240 --> 01:11:56.880
What Nawab was referring to in the video
could be something
completely unconnected, right?

1028
01:11:57.160 --> 01:11:59.560
Look here, officer.
Let's not beat around the bush.

1029
01:11:59.800 --> 01:12:01.440
<b>Our records are clean.</b>

1030
01:12:01.680 --> 01:12:03.760
<b>We are ready to cooperate with you.</b>

1031
01:12:03.880 --> 01:12:06.040
<b>If you still suspect Capo...</b>

1032
01:12:06.240 --> 01:12:08.240
<b>arrest Nawab and conduct an enquiry...</b>

1033
01:12:08.280 --> 01:12:10.880
and declare to the whole world
that our Capo is a good
person.

1034
01:12:11.520 --> 01:12:14.520
I will arrest Nawab
if you tell me where you are hiding him.

1035
01:12:14.640 --> 01:12:15.520
<b>Sorry?</b>

1036
01:12:16.880 --> 01:12:21.000
Nawab went missing 10 minutes
after we received the video.

1037
01:12:21.440 --> 01:12:22.760
<b>Tell me where he is.</b>

1038
01:12:22.880 --> 01:12:24.280
<b>Why are you asking us?</b>

1039
01:12:24.680 --> 01:12:26.040
<b>It's your job to find him!</b>

1040
01:12:26.120 --> 01:12:27.760
<b>Are you playing a game with me?</b>

1041
01:12:28.400 --> 01:12:29.880
<b>I'm almost there.</b>

1042
01:12:30.000 --> 01:12:32.520
<b>I won't spare any of you.</b>

1043
01:12:32.680 --> 01:12:36.000
I am going to hold your Capo
by his collar and drag him--

1044
01:12:36.120 --> 01:12:37.240
<b>Excuse me, officer!</b>

1045
01:12:37.440 --> 01:12:39.400
It will be nice if you can
maintain some decorum!

1046
01:12:39.400 --> 01:12:42.400
You don't get to run your mouth
because we treat you with
respect.

1047
01:12:42.400 --> 01:12:44.440
When the main witness goes missing
in a case as big as
this...

1048
01:12:44.440 --> 01:12:46.280
I can understand how frustrated
you must be.

1049
01:12:46.440 --> 01:12:47.920
<b>But don't you dare take it out on us.</b>

1050
01:12:48.040 --> 01:12:51.040
What you should do is
deploy a big team for this...

1051
01:12:51.160 --> 01:12:54.560
and search every country,
every city, every street out
there.

1052
01:12:54.640 --> 01:12:56.000
<b>Isn't that what you are paid for?</b>

1053
01:12:56.120 --> 01:12:58.400
It's the sweetest dish
I've had in my entire life.

1054
01:12:59.240 --> 01:13:01.000
<b>I'm all yours, Capo.</b>

1055
01:13:01.640 --> 01:13:03.640
<b>I'm missing you already.</b>

1056
01:13:08.560 --> 01:13:13.640
When a 22 year old punk
gets all this money and power...

1057
01:13:13.640 --> 01:13:18.520
I am just beginning to realise what
his corrupt little brain
 can be capable of.

1058
01:13:22.120 --> 01:13:23.520
<b>Actually you are right, officer.</b>

1059
01:13:24.240 --> 01:13:26.920
<b>My brain, my hands, my legs...</b>

1060
01:13:27.400 --> 01:13:30.520
and the lips that she just kissed
are just 22 years old.

1061
01:13:31.680 --> 01:13:36.520
But the blood that runs in my veins
has been doing corporate
 business for 120 years.

1062
01:13:37.040 --> 01:13:39.160
We know what to do
and how to do it.

1063
01:13:39.440 --> 01:13:40.440
<b>Buzz off!</b>

1064
01:13:40.520 --> 01:13:42.240
<b>Capo, no!</b>

1065
01:13:42.400 --> 01:13:44.560
Please, Capo.
Don't...

1066
01:13:44.800 --> 01:13:46.400
<b>Please, no...</b>

1067
01:13:47.880 --> 01:13:50.520
I'll buy out the CBI
and make you my employee!

1068
01:13:51.040 --> 01:13:52.880
<b>Capo, he is from the Interpol.</b>

1069
01:13:53.400 --> 01:13:54.520
What?
- Yeah...

1070
01:13:54.880 --> 01:13:56.000
<b>Shit!</b>

1071
01:13:56.520 --> 01:13:57.880
<b>That hurts, man.</b>

1072
01:14:03.120 --> 01:14:04.760
<b>What have you done, Uncle?</b>

1073
01:14:05.040 --> 01:14:06.760
Random guys are coming
and threatening me!

1074
01:14:06.760 --> 01:14:08.880
Sorry, Rishi.
I was very careful.

1075
01:14:09.120 --> 01:14:11.400
But I don't know where and how
it got leaked.

1076
01:14:11.520 --> 01:14:12.640
<b>Champagne, uncle?</b>

1077
01:14:12.680 --> 01:14:13.680
<b>No thanks.</b>

1078
01:14:13.880 --> 01:14:14.920
<b>Oh, come on.</b>

1079
01:14:15.560 --> 01:14:17.000
<b>Who is this Nellaiappan?</b>

1080
01:14:17.680 --> 01:14:19.120
<b>Since when have you had this link?</b>

1081
01:14:19.240 --> 01:14:23.240
About six years ago, you'd asked me to
finish off an
important witness in a jail in Ukraine.

1082
01:14:23.880 --> 01:14:25.400
<b>That wasn't an easy job.</b>

1083
01:14:25.760 --> 01:14:27.400
We got it done through
Nellai's guy.

1084
01:14:28.120 --> 01:14:31.520
Since then, we have been using
only Nellaiappan and his guy
to kill people.

1085
01:14:31.880 --> 01:14:33.640
<b>And who is this guy?</b>

1086
01:14:35.880 --> 01:14:36.880
<b>I don't know.</b>

1087
01:14:37.520 --> 01:14:38.400
<b>What?</b>

1088
01:14:38.520 --> 01:14:39.760
<b>I don't know who he is.</b>

1089
01:14:39.880 --> 01:14:41.680
I tried to find out who he is
several times.

1090
01:14:41.760 --> 01:14:42.880
<b>But I couldn't.</b>

1091
01:14:44.920 --> 01:14:46.520
<b>Does that guy know about us?</b>

1092
01:14:48.760 --> 01:14:49.760
<b>He does.</b>

1093
01:14:51.000 --> 01:14:52.000
<b>Wow!</b>

1094
01:14:52.280 --> 01:14:53.760
<b>That's so cool.</b>

1095
01:14:56.240 --> 01:15:00.760
So, who is this guy passing information
to the Interpol?

1096
01:15:02.520 --> 01:15:03.520
<b>I don't know.</b>

1097
01:15:04.800 --> 01:15:06.040
<b>You don't know anything!</b>

1098
01:15:10.760 --> 01:15:13.520
Uncle, do you remember
what you always said?

1099
01:15:14.000 --> 01:15:16.120
That you would be honest
with me and the company.

1100
01:15:16.520 --> 01:15:17.920
<b>And that you'd do anything for us.</b>

1101
01:15:18.520 --> 01:15:19.520
<b>So sweet!</b>

1102
01:15:20.240 --> 01:15:22.760
Uncle, you must be, what,
65 years old now?

1103
01:15:23.440 --> 01:15:25.640
Oh yeah, we just celebrated
your birthday!

1104
01:15:25.880 --> 01:15:28.440
<b>So you hardly have another 7-10 years left.</b>

1105
01:15:29.400 --> 01:15:31.000
<b>Give up those 10 years for me, uncle.</b>

1106
01:15:31.520 --> 01:15:32.520
<b>Rishi!</b>

1107
01:15:32.920 --> 01:15:34.280
<b>Rishi, what are you saying?</b>

1108
01:15:34.640 --> 01:15:35.880
<b>You're joking, right?</b>

1109
01:15:36.000 --> 01:15:37.440
No, uncle.
I'm very serious!

1110
01:15:37.640 --> 01:15:39.160
<b>Now it's all gone beyond limits.</b>

1111
01:15:39.240 --> 01:15:41.800
This is the only way we can
fix things, uncle. Please!

1112
01:15:41.920 --> 01:15:44.120
It's just 10 years, uncle.
Give it up!

1113
01:15:44.400 --> 01:15:46.280
Rishi, don't hurt me.
- Oh, no!

1114
01:15:46.400 --> 01:15:49.280
I'll just go away somewhere. Please, Rishi...
- Uncle,
please don't beg me like this.

1115
01:15:49.440 --> 01:15:51.240
Please, uncle.
- Please don't hurt me, Rishi.

1116
01:15:51.400 --> 01:15:53.640
Make sure he doesn't feel any pain.
- I won't say a word to
anyone.

1117
01:15:53.680 --> 01:15:55.160
<b>My dear uncle.</b>

1118
01:15:55.240 --> 01:15:56.760
Please, uncle.
- Rishi, please spare me.

1119
01:15:56.800 --> 01:15:58.120
Don't do it!
- Rishi...

1120
01:15:58.240 --> 01:15:59.760
No, no, no.
Uncle, please.

1121
01:15:59.760 --> 01:16:02.000
I'm already high
and having a bad trip.

1122
01:16:02.000 --> 01:16:05.000
Please don't do this, uncle.
It makes me very uncomfortable.

1123
01:16:05.240 --> 01:16:07.520
<b>Uncle, this is feeling terrible.</b>

1124
01:16:07.640 --> 01:16:09.880
Just hold steady and be still,
I'll finish it off quickly.

1125
01:16:10.000 --> 01:16:11.760
<b>Please, uncle!</b>

1126
01:16:12.760 --> 01:16:14.760
Oh, damn.
I warned you, didn't I?

1127
01:16:14.880 --> 01:16:17.400
I told you I was high
and asked you to stay still!

1128
01:16:33.280 --> 01:16:35.520
<b>Nellaiappan, the assassin...</b>

1129
01:16:36.000 --> 01:16:39.120
and that freak who is giving tip offs
from the outside...

1130
01:16:39.520 --> 01:16:40.760
<b>none of them should live.</b>

1131
01:16:41.640 --> 01:16:43.640
<b>Just clean up everything.</b>

1132
01:16:44.640 --> 01:16:46.280
<b>Every god-damn thing.</b>

1133
01:16:59.400 --> 01:17:02.000
Baby... the breeze is
so cold, isn't it?

1134
01:17:11.120 --> 01:17:13.120
I'll get us a cab.
Stay right here.

1135
01:17:14.240 --> 01:17:15.240
<b>Listen...</b>

1136
01:17:15.640 --> 01:17:18.000
I'll get us a cab.
Stay right here.

1137
01:17:31.520 --> 01:17:32.880
<b>Don't buy that newspaper.</b>

1138
01:17:36.640 --> 01:17:38.520
<b>Do you realise what you are doing?</b>

1139
01:17:39.240 --> 01:17:40.400
<b>Don't do this.</b>

1140
01:17:40.400 --> 01:17:42.640
You are killing random people
for total strangers.

1141
01:17:42.760 --> 01:17:44.520
<b>They are using you.</b>

1142
01:17:44.880 --> 01:17:46.000
<b>You are a good person.</b>

1143
01:17:46.040 --> 01:17:47.640
<b>Only I know that.</b>

1144
01:17:47.760 --> 01:17:51.000
It's not fair to dwell on the past
and make another woman
suffer for it.

1145
01:17:51.120 --> 01:17:53.400
You know I am saying this
for your own good, don't you?

1146
01:17:53.880 --> 01:17:55.520
<b>This isn't the life for you.</b>

1147
01:17:56.640 --> 01:17:58.920
<b>You should be with Bhavana.</b>

1148
01:17:59.400 --> 01:18:01.040
<b>That is where your life lies.</b>

1149
01:18:01.240 --> 01:18:03.520
<b>Let's leave all of this behind.</b>

1150
01:18:03.640 --> 01:18:05.680
Stop, don't do it.
Listen to me.

1151
01:18:05.880 --> 01:18:09.000
Think about everything we've lost
to get the life we wanted.

1152
01:18:12.800 --> 01:18:13.800
<b>Please!</b>

1153
01:18:57.400 --> 01:18:58.400
<b>See...</b>

1154
01:18:58.640 --> 01:19:00.520
<b>you are shedding tears.</b>

1155
01:19:00.760 --> 01:19:02.040
<b>This is who you are.</b>

1156
01:19:02.120 --> 01:19:05.120
Knowingly or unknowingly,
don't make another mistake.

1157
01:19:05.560 --> 01:19:07.920
<b>Let's go and get Bhavana.</b>

1158
01:19:11.280 --> 01:19:12.400
<b>Stop here.</b>

1159
01:19:14.640 --> 01:19:17.000
Mathi, wait!
Where are you going?

1160
01:19:42.760 --> 01:19:45.760
For the first time,
I am in your place.

1161
01:19:48.040 --> 01:19:50.400
<b>I finally understand the pain.</b>

1162
01:19:53.880 --> 01:19:56.400
You said you'd never leave
even if I tell you to.

1163
01:19:58.440 --> 01:19:59.880
<b>I just want to ask three questions.</b>

1164
01:20:01.000 --> 01:20:02.240
<b>Then I'll leave.</b>

1165
01:20:05.880 --> 01:20:07.920
If I tell you we don't need
anyone's permission...

1166
01:20:08.280 --> 01:20:09.800
<b>and ask you to come with me now...</b>

1167
01:20:11.240 --> 01:20:13.040
<b>will you come with me or not?</b>

1168
01:20:15.800 --> 01:20:21.400
If I tell you that I won't let you down
for a hundred
years...

1169
01:20:23.160 --> 01:20:25.520
<b>will you come with me or not?</b>

1170
01:20:29.400 --> 01:20:36.280
If I tell you I will never ask you to leave
even if my life
depends on it...

1171
01:20:39.240 --> 01:20:40.440
<b>will you...</b>

1172
01:20:42.760 --> 01:20:44.000
<b>come with me?</b>

1173
01:20:47.000 --> 01:20:47.880
<b>Or not?</b>

1174
01:20:51.160 --> 01:20:52.280
<b>She will come with you.</b>

1175
01:20:53.040 --> 01:20:55.120
If she doesn't,
I will convince her.

1176
01:20:57.400 --> 01:20:58.520
<b>Go, Bhavana.</b>

1177
01:21:11.880 --> 01:21:14.520
<b>♪ Fireworks and drumbeats ♪</b>

1178
01:21:14.760 --> 01:21:17.120
<b>♪ Fireworks and drumbeats ♪</b>

1179
01:21:18.040 --> 01:21:23.240
♪ Like a sweet, magical, floral breeze ♪
♪ She wafted into
my life ♪

1180
01:21:24.000 --> 01:21:26.000
♪ Jubilation! ♪
♪ Jubilation, jubilation! ♪

1181
01:21:26.120 --> 01:21:28.240
<b>♪ Oh, jubilation... ♪</b>

1182
01:21:32.760 --> 01:21:36.240
♪ Hey Dragonfly ♪
♪ Don't you bounce ♪

1183
01:21:38.240 --> 01:21:41.760
<b>♪ Don't you bounce today, Dragonfly ♪</b>

1184
01:21:44.400 --> 01:21:49.520
♪ Hey Tinkling Bells ♪
♪ Bow down to him ♪

1185
01:21:50.280 --> 01:21:55.800
♪ It's only me, me, and me ♪
♪ I'm the only one in his life
♪

1186
01:21:56.120 --> 01:22:01.240
<b>♪ You're the reason behind my naughty smile ♪</b>

1187
01:22:04.880 --> 01:22:08.560
♪ Hey Dragonfly ♪
♪ Don't you bounce ♪

1188
01:22:10.760 --> 01:22:14.280
<b>♪ Don't you bounce today, Dragonfly ♪</b>

1189
01:22:20.920 --> 01:22:24.640
General, we found cyanide needles
in the cameras we seized.

1190
01:22:24.920 --> 01:22:29.920
He's imported this cyanide and some other gadgets
through
different forms from Finland.

1191
01:22:30.520 --> 01:22:31.520
<b>Not just this.</b>

1192
01:22:31.640 --> 01:22:34.240
He had planned a big blast
at the old venue.

1193
01:22:34.680 --> 01:22:37.040
It's just a matter of time, General.
I'll get him.

1194
01:23:01.000 --> 01:23:07.400
♪ I watched my life pass me by ♪
♪ With no rhyme or meaning
♪

1195
01:23:08.120 --> 01:23:14.240
♪ The moment I found you ♪
♪ I found the meaning to life ♪

1196
01:23:15.640 --> 01:23:21.040
♪ I'll be the life in your body ♪
♪ And never part you, even
 for a moment ♪

1197
01:23:21.440 --> 01:23:25.800
♪ I'll hold your hand forever ♪
♪ Unfaltering, always ♪

1198
01:23:26.040 --> 01:23:30.640
♪ This handsome gentleman is here ♪
♪ But his heart is with
the pretty lady ♪

1199
01:23:30.800 --> 01:23:35.760
♪ He cannot hear our voices ♪
♪ Let's fire a cannon ♪

1200
01:23:36.000 --> 01:23:39.880
♪ You must birth a hundred children ♪
♪ Oh, no! That won't
do ♪

1201
01:23:39.920 --> 01:23:42.880
<b>♪ Our population growth is dependent on you ♪</b>

1202
01:23:42.880 --> 01:23:45.760
♪ Hey Dragonfly ♪
♪ Don't you bounce ♪

1203
01:23:48.240 --> 01:23:52.000
<b>♪ Don't you bounce today, Dragonfly ♪</b>

1204
01:23:54.400 --> 01:23:59.440
♪ Hey Tinkling Bells ♪
♪ Bow down to him ♪

1205
01:24:00.440 --> 01:24:05.760
♪ It's only me, me, and me ♪
♪ I'm the only one in his life
♪

1206
01:24:06.280 --> 01:24:12.000
<b>♪ You're the reason behind my naughty smile ♪</b>

1207
01:24:53.640 --> 01:24:54.880
<b>So, teacher...</b>

1208
01:24:55.040 --> 01:24:56.120
<b>Have you eaten?</b>

1209
01:24:56.760 --> 01:24:58.760
What about you, teacher?
Have you eaten?

1210
01:24:58.760 --> 01:25:00.680
Hey, Judy...
aren't you sleeping yet?

1211
01:25:00.760 --> 01:25:02.880
I was unable to fall asleep.
So I just went for a walk.

1212
01:25:02.920 --> 01:25:04.240
<b>You know Judy, don't you?</b>

1213
01:25:04.400 --> 01:25:06.400
<b>She is my most favourite student.</b>

1214
01:25:06.920 --> 01:25:09.000
<b>Maybe you don't know about us.</b>

1215
01:25:09.120 --> 01:25:11.440
<b>But we know a lot about you.</b>

1216
01:25:12.120 --> 01:25:14.240
You made her lament
quite a bit!

1217
01:25:16.120 --> 01:25:17.120
<b>So...</b>

1218
01:25:17.640 --> 01:25:20.640
<b>I heard you are scary good at maths!</b>

1219
01:25:21.240 --> 01:25:22.520
<b>Oh, I forgot to mention...</b>

1220
01:25:22.760 --> 01:25:24.000
<b>She is not from criminology.</b>

1221
01:25:24.120 --> 01:25:25.440
<b>She is a mathematician.</b>

1222
01:25:25.640 --> 01:25:29.120
She is working with the Interpol
on a really big case at the
 moment.

1223
01:25:30.000 --> 01:25:30.920
<b>Oh...</b>

1224
01:25:31.000 --> 01:25:31.880
<b>Nice!</b>

1225
01:25:32.680 --> 01:25:35.280
Are you wondering what's the connection
between maths and
crime?

1226
01:25:35.760 --> 01:25:38.120
<b>There is this genius mathematician!</b>

1227
01:25:38.640 --> 01:25:41.640
He is using maths to carry out
several assassinations...

1228
01:25:41.680 --> 01:25:43.000
<b>and he is getting away with it!</b>

1229
01:25:43.240 --> 01:25:45.160
<b>We are trying to find him.</b>

1230
01:25:45.400 --> 01:25:47.040
<b>Judy, I wanted to ask you...</b>

1231
01:25:47.160 --> 01:25:49.120
<b>how did your Russia visit go?</b>

1232
01:25:49.160 --> 01:25:50.520
<b>Oh, ma'am...</b>

1233
01:25:50.640 --> 01:25:52.800
<b>it was perfectly setup, ma'am.</b>

1234
01:25:52.880 --> 01:25:54.400
<b>Like, perfect!</b>

1235
01:25:54.640 --> 01:25:56.280
<b>There is this hacker.</b>

1236
01:25:56.400 --> 01:26:00.800
He's been feeding information to the Interpol
all along
using this joker character.

1237
01:26:00.880 --> 01:26:03.400
We used that information
and almost got to him.

1238
01:26:03.560 --> 01:26:05.640
<b>We were that close to him.</b>

1239
01:26:05.880 --> 01:26:07.040
<b>That close!</b>

1240
01:26:08.760 --> 01:26:12.240
Finally, we couldn't even get
a hair strand as evidence.

1241
01:26:13.240 --> 01:26:14.880
<b>Cobra is the real deal, ma'am.</b>

1242
01:26:15.680 --> 01:26:16.760
<b>Just, wow.</b>

1243
01:26:17.520 --> 01:26:19.120
Cobra!
- That's enough. Leave now.

1244
01:26:19.400 --> 01:26:21.000
<b>Okay, you guys carry on!</b>

1245
01:26:21.120 --> 01:26:22.120
<b>Bye!</b>

1246
01:26:23.520 --> 01:26:24.920
<b>Okay, the time is...</b>

1247
01:26:25.000 --> 01:26:26.920
<b>What sort of dress sense is this?</b>

1248
01:26:26.920 --> 01:26:28.520
<b>With your shirt tucked in!</b>

1249
01:26:29.240 --> 01:26:30.640
<b>Why are you squirming?</b>

1250
01:26:30.880 --> 01:26:34.040
If you start squirming or shying away
when I come close to
you...

1251
01:26:34.240 --> 01:26:35.520
<b>I'll kill you!</b>

1252
01:26:36.240 --> 01:26:37.400
<b>You see this?</b>

1253
01:26:37.640 --> 01:26:40.880
You are registered as my property now.
You are done for!

1254
01:26:41.240 --> 01:26:44.680
That is the first thing that should
come to your mind when
you see this!

1255
01:26:44.920 --> 01:26:45.880
<b>Okay?</b>

1256
01:26:49.240 --> 01:26:50.160
<b>It's beautiful.</b>

1257
01:26:50.760 --> 01:26:51.920
<b>Look at that!</b>

1258
01:26:52.640 --> 01:26:54.640
I had no idea
you notice and admire these things!

1259
01:26:57.280 --> 01:26:59.240
It will turn into a
deeper shade of red tomorrow.

1260
01:27:01.400 --> 01:27:04.880
It will look beautiful during the wedding
when it turns into
 a deeper shade of red.

1261
01:27:06.760 --> 01:27:08.000
<b>Damn you, grandpa!</b>

1262
01:27:08.520 --> 01:27:11.120
I need to break his TV already!
- Let me take care of it.

1263
01:27:11.240 --> 01:27:15.880
[news] On account of the official visit
of Japanese
diplomats to Kolkata...

1264
01:27:16.000 --> 01:27:20.240
an emergency council meeting has been scheduled
under the
leadership of DGP Ganguly.

1265
01:27:20.760 --> 01:27:25.120
At the house of Hindustan Today's senior
journalist
Nellaiyappan in Kumurtali, Kolkata...

1266
01:27:25.400 --> 01:27:29.680
three family members were found dead
after they consumed
poison and committed suicide.

1267
01:27:29.760 --> 01:27:35.760
The police have setup a special team
to search for the
missing Nellaiyappan.

1268
01:27:35.880 --> 01:27:38.120
They are also questioning people
close to him.

1269
01:27:38.120 --> 01:27:39.160
<b>I know him very well.</b>

1270
01:27:39.240 --> 01:27:42.400
He didn't have any debts.
He actually had a lot of savings.

1271
01:27:42.520 --> 01:27:44.880
But now they are saying
he's got no money in his account.

1272
01:27:45.000 --> 01:27:46.400
<b>Something is wrong.</b>

1273
01:27:46.400 --> 01:27:48.760
The police are cooking up some story
to divert this case.

1274
01:27:48.880 --> 01:27:51.120
The truth will come out
only if we find Nellai Sir.

1275
01:27:54.000 --> 01:27:58.400
I knew the Interpol guy was going to
sniff everything out.

1276
01:27:58.520 --> 01:28:00.000
<b>And now he is nearing us.</b>

1277
01:28:00.760 --> 01:28:02.440
<b>If it was the Interpol...</b>

1278
01:28:02.520 --> 01:28:05.520
they would have arrested him
and gone down the legal route.

1279
01:28:05.680 --> 01:28:07.920
<b>But that's not what happened.</b>

1280
01:28:08.240 --> 01:28:10.120
<b>Nellai is in some trouble.</b>

1281
01:28:10.120 --> 01:28:11.640
<b>Oh, I see!</b>

1282
01:28:11.640 --> 01:28:14.280
Maybe that was what he was trying
to say through the
newspaper, Dad?

1283
01:28:15.880 --> 01:28:17.280
<b>Did we make a mistake?</b>

1284
01:28:24.880 --> 01:28:27.400
Do you have the Hindustan Today newspaper
dated December
27th?

1285
01:28:27.640 --> 01:28:29.120
You want a newspaper
from two days ago?

1286
01:28:29.120 --> 01:28:31.240
We don't keep it here.
It's at the warehouse.

1287
01:28:31.240 --> 01:28:32.240
<b>Where is that?</b>

1288
01:28:32.280 --> 01:28:34.160
<b>Take a left turn there.</b>

1289
01:28:40.440 --> 01:28:43.880
Hello, excuse me. The newspapers--
- Everything is in there.

1290
01:28:43.880 --> 01:28:45.240
Hindustan...
- In there.

1291
01:28:45.560 --> 01:28:47.240
<b>Go and take it for yourself.</b>

1292
01:29:44.640 --> 01:29:47.160
Does this mean he sent some details
through this mail, Dad?

1293
01:29:47.240 --> 01:29:48.120
<b>No way!</b>

1294
01:29:48.120 --> 01:29:49.240
<b>No chance at all.</b>

1295
01:29:49.240 --> 01:29:54.280
He knows we will never use mail or phones
under any
circumstances for safety reasons.

1296
01:29:54.400 --> 01:29:55.400
<b>Something is wrong.</b>

1297
01:29:55.440 --> 01:29:59.560
Maybe he was in a situation where
the only option he had was
 to send a mail.

1298
01:29:59.640 --> 01:30:01.400
<b>No, this is not safe.</b>

1299
01:30:01.440 --> 01:30:02.880
<b>Something is fishy!</b>

1300
01:30:02.880 --> 01:30:04.440
<b>We have no idea what happened to Nellai.</b>

1301
01:30:04.520 --> 01:30:06.680
Three people are dead
at his house.

1302
01:30:06.760 --> 01:30:08.880
Are we still going to go on
and on about safety...

1303
01:30:08.920 --> 01:30:11.760
or are we going to try to find out
what happened at his
house?

1304
01:30:20.000 --> 01:30:22.240
The shop shuts in 30 minutes.
Hurry up. - Yeah, okay.

1305
01:31:21.400 --> 01:31:22.400
<b>Hello?</b>

1306
01:31:22.400 --> 01:31:25.640
<b>Mic testing 1,2, 3.</b>

1307
01:31:26.640 --> 01:31:27.880
<b>Do you recognise him?</b>

1308
01:31:28.400 --> 01:31:30.440
<b>Your wonderful godfather!</b>

1309
01:31:31.160 --> 01:31:33.880
It looks like he is getting
a nice massage, doesn't it?

1310
01:31:34.560 --> 01:31:35.640
<b>No!</b>

1311
01:31:35.880 --> 01:31:39.120
<b>This is called Chinese water torture.</b>

1312
01:31:40.040 --> 01:31:44.880
When the water falls
drop after drop after drop...

1313
01:31:45.040 --> 01:31:46.880
<b>it can even dent a rock, you know?</b>

1314
01:31:47.400 --> 01:31:50.920
So imagine, if it can deform a rock,
what would happen to
your old man's head?

1315
01:31:53.520 --> 01:31:55.000
<b>As time passes...</b>

1316
01:31:55.000 --> 01:31:57.560
every drop that falls on his head
will feel like...

1317
01:31:57.680 --> 01:31:58.640
<b>boom!</b>

1318
01:31:59.120 --> 01:32:00.160
<b>Boom!</b>

1319
01:32:00.160 --> 01:32:01.640
<b>It will feel like thunder.</b>

1320
01:32:02.000 --> 01:32:06.000
His mind will be consumed with fear
about the next drop that
 would fall on him.

1321
01:32:07.560 --> 01:32:08.640
<b>Boom!</b>

1322
01:32:09.760 --> 01:32:12.160
<b>Slowly but surely...</b>

1323
01:32:12.240 --> 01:32:13.800
<b>his brain's rhythm will break...</b>

1324
01:32:13.800 --> 01:32:17.040
<b>and he will lose his consciousness!</b>

1325
01:32:17.880 --> 01:32:19.880
<b>Then the old man will blurt everything out.</b>

1326
01:32:20.040 --> 01:32:21.240
<b>Everything.</b>

1327
01:32:21.680 --> 01:32:23.760
<b>Every single secret.</b>

1328
01:32:27.800 --> 01:32:29.040
<b>Oh, I forgot to mention...</b>

1329
01:32:29.120 --> 01:32:33.000
other than you, the CBI are also
watching this video as we
speak.

1330
01:32:34.800 --> 01:32:36.760
Who is this?
Who sent this to us?

1331
01:32:36.800 --> 01:32:39.000
Don't know, sir.
An unknown ID shared this link.

1332
01:32:39.040 --> 01:32:40.400
<b>It's streaming on the dark web.</b>

1333
01:32:40.440 --> 01:32:42.560
Only those who know about this link
can open it.

1334
01:32:42.760 --> 01:32:44.120
<b>Forward this link to me.</b>

1335
01:32:44.160 --> 01:32:46.400
<b>Hey, don't worry!</b>

1336
01:32:46.560 --> 01:32:48.440
<b>I won't rat you out so easily.</b>

1337
01:32:48.520 --> 01:32:50.880
This old man isn't going
to speak up easily either.

1338
01:32:52.240 --> 01:32:55.400
<b>5 seconds into 2 feet height...</b>

1339
01:32:55.440 --> 01:32:58.880
into 3600 seconds
divided by 5...

1340
01:32:59.040 --> 01:33:00.760
<b>plus, plus what...</b>

1341
01:33:00.800 --> 01:33:03.120
<b>plus this guy's age!</b>

1342
01:33:04.120 --> 01:33:06.680
<b>I don't know how to calculate this.</b>

1343
01:33:06.920 --> 01:33:08.880
<b>You are good at maths, aren't you?</b>

1344
01:33:09.120 --> 01:33:13.400
<b>I think you only have about 30-31 hours.</b>

1345
01:33:13.640 --> 01:33:17.040
Before that, try to save
this old man's life if you can...

1346
01:33:17.160 --> 01:33:19.280
<b>and save yourself too, okay?</b>

1347
01:33:26.040 --> 01:33:27.560
<b>I don't know who you are.</b>

1348
01:33:29.160 --> 01:33:30.760
<b>But I can see I am your target.</b>

1349
01:33:32.000 --> 01:33:33.880
You thought you were
attacking me...

1350
01:33:34.880 --> 01:33:36.880
but you've stepped into
a quagmire instead.

1351
01:33:37.440 --> 01:33:39.000
<b>A quagmire named Rishi Corp.</b>

1352
01:33:44.160 --> 01:33:47.920
<b>Thirty hours to go!</b>

1353
01:33:52.520 --> 01:33:54.520
You have no idea
how dangerous he is.

1354
01:33:54.880 --> 01:33:56.240
<b>He will definitely--</b>

1355
01:34:04.640 --> 01:34:05.680
<b>What?</b>

1356
01:34:05.880 --> 01:34:07.000
<b>Are you trying to scare me?</b>

1357
01:34:12.520 --> 01:34:13.800
<b>You math head...</b>

1358
01:34:14.680 --> 01:34:16.280
<b>your calculations won't work with me.</b>

1359
01:34:17.000 --> 01:34:18.520
<b>I don't care about anything.</b>

1360
01:34:19.240 --> 01:34:20.680
<b>Not even death.</b>

1361
01:34:21.120 --> 01:34:22.520
<b>All I need is you.</b>

1362
01:34:23.640 --> 01:34:26.120
I want to watch you
run for your life and die.

1363
01:34:29.880 --> 01:34:31.680
<b>Your countdown begins now.</b>

1364
01:34:34.400 --> 01:34:35.280
<b>Run!</b>

1365
01:34:35.760 --> 01:34:37.120
<b>I said, run!</b>

1366
01:34:47.680 --> 01:34:50.000
I just got a call saying
they found our car at the airport.

1367
01:34:50.120 --> 01:34:51.400
<b>The groom isn't there.</b>

1368
01:34:51.520 --> 01:34:54.520
They said they'd talk to the airlines
and find out which
city he's gone to.

1369
01:34:55.040 --> 01:34:56.240
<b>He's left the city?</b>

1370
01:34:57.520 --> 01:34:58.640
<b>What is this, Kumaresan?</b>

1371
01:34:58.760 --> 01:35:00.760
We are just two hours away
from the wedding.

1372
01:35:00.880 --> 01:35:03.240
<b>The guests have started to come in.</b>

1373
01:35:03.800 --> 01:35:05.120
<b>What is this, brother?</b>

1374
01:35:06.000 --> 01:35:08.120
<b>Why can't I ever understand him?</b>

1375
01:35:08.880 --> 01:35:10.880
<b>Things were going just fine.</b>

1376
01:35:12.800 --> 01:35:14.440
<b>Did I say something wrong?</b>

1377
01:35:15.160 --> 01:35:16.760
<b>Or do something wrong?</b>

1378
01:35:17.240 --> 01:35:20.400
Or did I just pester him
into agreeing to this marriage?

1379
01:35:21.760 --> 01:35:22.760
<b>But, no.</b>

1380
01:35:23.440 --> 01:35:24.880
<b>He was the one who came to me.</b>

1381
01:35:26.000 --> 01:35:28.680
No, I'm sure he went
on some emergency.

1382
01:35:29.440 --> 01:35:31.120
<b>But is he safe?</b>

1383
01:35:31.520 --> 01:35:33.280
Can you please find out
what happened to him?

1384
01:35:33.280 --> 01:35:35.240
Why do you care
what happens to him anymore?

1385
01:35:39.120 --> 01:35:40.880
<b>How can you say that, brother?</b>

1386
01:35:42.240 --> 01:35:43.400
<b>You don't need him.</b>

1387
01:35:44.000 --> 01:35:45.400
<b>He isn't right for you.</b>

1388
01:35:48.400 --> 01:35:51.520
I don't mean to say
he is a bad person.

1389
01:35:53.520 --> 01:35:55.640
He is just not able
to accept you, Bhavana.

1390
01:35:58.520 --> 01:36:00.000
<b>Fifteen years ago...</b>

1391
01:36:01.120 --> 01:36:03.640
I met Mathi in Kolkata
for the first time.

1392
01:36:04.240 --> 01:36:05.760
<b>He didn't know me back then.</b>

1393
01:36:07.400 --> 01:36:08.760
<b>But the whole neighbourhood...</b>

1394
01:36:09.920 --> 01:36:12.240
<b>knew him and Jennifer very well.</b>

1395
01:36:13.400 --> 01:36:14.440
<b>Jennifer?</b>

1396
01:36:15.920 --> 01:36:16.920
<b>Yes.</b>

1397
01:36:18.040 --> 01:36:20.120
<b>Mathi was in love with Jennifer.</b>

1398
01:36:21.120 --> 01:36:22.560
<b>Sincerely.</b>

1399
01:36:23.800 --> 01:36:25.880
<b>I don't know who jinxed it.</b>

1400
01:37:05.520 --> 01:37:07.560
<b>They said you are perfectly fine.</b>

1401
01:37:07.640 --> 01:37:11.400
Sign this statement which says you are fine
and get going.

1402
01:37:11.520 --> 01:37:14.760
<b>Sir, my phone got lost somewhere.</b>

1403
01:37:14.800 --> 01:37:16.760
<b>Let's talk about that later.</b>

1404
01:37:16.800 --> 01:37:18.240
<b>This concerns the Commissioner's daughter.</b>

1405
01:37:18.280 --> 01:37:19.240
<b>Sign now.</b>

1406
01:37:19.240 --> 01:37:21.240
But, sir...
- Just sign it, man.

1407
01:37:21.280 --> 01:37:22.440
<b>Get his signature.</b>

1408
01:37:22.440 --> 01:37:24.120
<b>Just sign it, kid.</b>

1409
01:37:32.680 --> 01:37:33.640
<b>Sir...</b>

1410
01:37:34.240 --> 01:37:35.240
<b>Sir!</b>

1411
01:37:36.000 --> 01:37:37.000
<b>My leg...</b>

1412
01:37:37.760 --> 01:37:38.680
<b>Doctor!</b>

1413
01:37:41.800 --> 01:37:43.240
Has he signed?
- Yes, sir.

1414
01:37:43.400 --> 01:37:44.400
<b>Wait outside.</b>

1415
01:37:45.440 --> 01:37:46.520
<b>Daddy, this is not fair.</b>

1416
01:37:46.520 --> 01:37:48.160
We should take care
of his treatment.

1417
01:37:48.240 --> 01:37:49.440
<b>How can we just leave him like this?</b>

1418
01:37:49.520 --> 01:37:50.640
<b>You shut up, Jenny.</b>

1419
01:37:50.760 --> 01:37:54.120
She hits some random guy on the road
and insists on treating
 him at a big hospital!

1420
01:37:54.240 --> 01:37:56.520
I should have thought about this
before giving you the car.

1421
01:37:56.520 --> 01:37:58.120
Discharge him
and send him away, Indu.

1422
01:37:59.040 --> 01:38:00.560
No, aunty.
Please don't listen to him.

1423
01:38:00.640 --> 01:38:01.880
<b>Treat him, aunty.</b>

1424
01:38:02.000 --> 01:38:03.760
<b>You say it's a serious fracture too.</b>

1425
01:38:03.800 --> 01:38:05.880
I'll pay you later.
No, actually...

1426
01:38:06.760 --> 01:38:10.640
ئەمە بگرە، و تکایە چارەسەری پێویست
بەو کوڕە ببەخشە.

1427
01:38:10.760 --> 01:38:12.520
<b>جینی، دەچی چی بکەیت!</b>

1428
01:38:12.760 --> 01:38:15.040
دەستبەندەکەی دایکت لەبیرەوەری ئەو
لە دەست دەکەیت.

1429
01:38:15.560 --> 01:38:17.520
تۆ ھەرگیز ئەمە داناگریت
بە ھیچ ھۆکارێک.

1430
01:38:19.920 --> 01:38:22.240
ئەو کوڕە کێیە؟
خۆشەویستتە؟

1431
01:38:23.520 --> 01:38:24.640
<b>دەی، خاڵۆژن.</b>

1432
01:38:24.680 --> 01:38:27.640
ئایا دەبێت خۆشەویستم بێت
یان هاوڕێیەک بۆ ئەوەی
یارمەتی دەرببڕم؟

1433
01:38:28.040 --> 01:38:28.920
<b>کەواتە چی؟</b>

1434
01:38:29.000 --> 01:38:30.120
<b>هەژارە، خاڵۆژن.</b>

1435
01:38:30.160 --> 01:38:32.160
چەند سەعاتێکە
بریندار بووە.

1436
01:38:32.240 --> 01:38:33.920
بەڵام تا ئێستا تەنانەت یەک کەسیش
نەهاتووە بۆ سەردانی.

1437
01:38:34.240 --> 01:38:36.880
<b>پێیان وتین کە هیچ کەسی نییە.</b>

1438
01:38:37.520 --> 01:38:39.520
<b>ئەگەر دایکی هێشتا لە ژیاندا بایە...</b>

1439
01:38:39.640 --> 01:38:42.880
پەشۆکاو دەبوو و ڕای دەکردە لێرە بۆ ئەوەی بزانێت کوڕەکەی
باشە یان نا.

1440
01:38:43.920 --> 01:38:46.120
<b>ھەست بە ناڕەحەتییەکی زۆر دەکەم بۆی.</b>

1441
01:38:47.880 --> 01:38:50.240
کەواتە تکایە،
زیاتر بیری لێ مەکەرەوە.

1442
01:38:50.280 --> 01:38:52.120
<b>تەنها ئەو نەشتەرگەرییەی پێویستە بۆی ئەنجام بدە.</b>

1443
01:38:52.240 --> 01:38:54.120
باشە، بەڵام سەرەتا دەبێت--
- ئەوە بگرە!

1444
01:38:54.160 --> 01:38:56.240
دوای ئەوەی بەهۆش خۆی هاتەوە،
تکایە ئەمە بدە پێی.

1445
01:38:56.280 --> 01:38:57.440
باشە، خاڵۆژن؟
خوات لەگەڵ.

1446
01:38:57.440 --> 01:38:59.120
<b>جینی، ئەمە ببەوە.</b>

1447
01:38:59.160 --> 01:39:00.240
<b>جینی!</b>

1448
01:39:03.240 --> 01:39:05.880
چایترا، ڕێکارەکانی کەیسی رووداوەکە تەواو بکە...

1449
01:39:05.920 --> 01:39:08.040
و بۆ نەشتەرگەری ئەمشەو ئامادەبە.
- باشە، دکتۆر.

1450
01:39:17.680 --> 01:39:18.560
<b>دەی!</b>

1451
01:39:20.440 --> 01:39:22.440
<b>ماسی، تۆ زۆر...</b>

1452
01:39:23.680 --> 01:39:24.880
<b>گەمژەی؟</b>

1453
01:39:26.560 --> 01:39:29.240
پێویست بوو مۆبایلەکەت بەکاربهێنیت
کاتێک لە شەقامەکە دەپەڕیتەوە،
گەمژە؟

1454
01:39:30.240 --> 01:39:32.800
بیری لێ بکەرەوە چی روودەدا
ئەگەر شێلابامایە!

1455
01:39:33.000 --> 01:39:34.440
<b>پێویست بوو ئەوە بکەم.</b>

1456
01:39:36.040 --> 01:39:38.240
دەزانیت چەندە حەزم لە
لێخوڕینی ئۆتۆمبێلە.

1457
01:39:38.560 --> 01:39:41.000
ئێستا بەهۆی تۆوە، ئیتر ناهێڵن
ئۆتۆمبێل لێخوڕینەوە.

1458
01:39:41.040 --> 01:39:42.800
<b>هەرگیز ئەمەت بۆ لێخۆش نابم.</b>

1459
01:39:43.240 --> 01:39:45.000
<b>بیستوومە هاوپۆلم بوویتە--</b>

1460
01:39:45.680 --> 01:39:46.760
<b>هاو--</b>

1461
01:39:47.120 --> 01:39:48.280
<b>هاوپۆل؟</b>

1462
01:39:49.400 --> 01:39:52.040
دەبێت بۆ ماوەی چوار ساڵی داهاتوو
هەرگیز نەبینم.

1463
01:39:52.400 --> 01:39:53.920
<b>هەرگیز نەکەویتە بەر چاوانم!</b>

1464
01:39:54.040 --> 01:39:55.040
<b>ڕقم لێیە.</b>

1465
01:39:55.120 --> 01:39:56.000
<b>ڕقم لێیە.</b>

1466
01:39:56.000 --> 01:39:56.880
<b>ڕقم لێیە.</b>

1467
01:40:14.640 --> 01:40:19.440
<b>♪ کاتێک لە دەوروبەرم نیت ♪</b>

1468
01:40:20.400 --> 01:40:25.120
<b>♪ من لە هیچ شوێنێک دیار نییم ♪</b>

1469
01:40:26.000 --> 01:40:31.000
<b>♪ کاتێک لە دەوروبەرم نیت ♪</b>

1470
01:40:31.680 --> 01:40:36.120
<b>♪ من لە هیچ شوێنێک دیار نییم ♪</b>

1471
01:40:36.440 --> 01:40:39.000
♪ گیانم دەڕژێت ♪
- ببەخشە.

1472
01:40:39.120 --> 01:40:41.880
♪ دڵم دەتوێتەوە ♪
- ببەخشە.

1473
01:40:42.120 --> 01:40:46.400
<b>♪ ئەی ئاسمانی من ♪</b>

1474
01:40:47.880 --> 01:40:55.880
<b>♪ تاکە کات کە تۆم بینی ♪</b>

1475
01:40:56.440 --> 01:41:01.120
♪ لە خۆشیدا ♪
♪ سەرسام بووم ♪

1476
01:41:02.000 --> 01:41:07.040
<b>♪ زمان لعل و بێ دەنگ بووم ♪</b>

1477
01:41:07.680 --> 01:41:15.560
♪ بۆچی لە یادەوەرییەکانمدا دەمێنێتەوە؟ ♪
♪ ئەی دایکە... ♪

1478
01:41:16.880 --> 01:41:21.400
<b>♪ کاتێک لە دەوروبەرم نیت ♪</b>

1479
01:41:25.680 --> 01:41:27.240
<b>تکایە چاوم پێدا مەگێڕە!</b>

1480
01:41:27.400 --> 01:41:28.520
<b>چاوەڕێی چی دەکەیت؟</b>

1481
01:41:28.520 --> 01:41:31.120
خێزانەکەم ئیتر ناهێڵن ئۆتۆمبێل لێخوڕین،
هەمووی بەهۆی
تۆوە!

1482
01:41:36.520 --> 01:41:38.920
<b>هەر کاتێک حەزت لە لێخوڕینی ئۆتۆمبێل بوو...</b>

1483
01:41:39.160 --> 01:41:40.560
<b>دەتوانیت ئەم ئۆتۆمبێلە ببەیت.</b>

1484
01:41:41.880 --> 01:41:43.040
<b>بەجدتە؟</b>

1485
01:41:44.760 --> 01:41:46.520
<b>بەڵام ناتوانم لە پۆلەکان هەڵبێم.</b>

1486
01:41:46.560 --> 01:41:48.640
دەربارەی ئامادەبوون چی--
- دەتوانین هاککی بکەین.

1487
01:41:56.400 --> 01:42:01.160
<b>♪ تۆ بارانی خۆرئاوای ♪</b>

1488
01:42:02.000 --> 01:42:06.880
<b>♪ وەرە، بەسەر مندا ببارە ♪</b>

1489
01:42:07.520 --> 01:42:12.440
<b>♪ چیڕۆکێک کە پێشتر هەرگیز نەگوتراوە ♪</b>

1490
01:42:13.240 --> 01:42:17.760
<b>♪ ئەشکەنجە وەک چێژ وایە ♪</b>

1491
01:42:18.920 --> 01:42:25.680
♪ ئاسکە سیحراوییەکەم ♪
♪ ڤینایە هۆشمەندەکەم ♪

1492
01:42:25.680 --> 01:42:29.280
<b>♪ تۆ نوێژی منی ♪</b>

1493
01:42:33.000 --> 01:42:37.920
<b>♪ کاتێک لە دەوروبەرم نیت ♪</b>

1494
01:42:38.680 --> 01:42:43.400
<b>♪ من لە هیچ شوێنێک دیار نییم ♪</b>

1495
01:43:12.640 --> 01:43:17.880
<b>♪ ئەو قژە ڕەشە شەپۆلاوییەی تۆ ♪</b>

1496
01:43:18.240 --> 01:43:23.760
<b>♪ بۆچی منی تێدا هەڵدەگریت؟ ♪</b>

1497
01:43:23.920 --> 01:43:29.240
<b>♪ پێش ئەوەی بکەومە سەر زەوی ♪</b>

1498
01:43:29.640 --> 01:43:34.880
<b>♪ تۆ ئەو کەسە بوویت کە گرتیتە دەست ♪</b>

1499
01:43:35.160 --> 01:43:40.760
♪ وەک لانکە دەتجوڵانم ♪
♪ لە باوەش خۆتدا دەتجۆڵیەوە ♪

1500
01:43:40.880 --> 01:43:45.680
<b>♪ بۆچی چاوەڕێی ئەو ڕۆژانەت کرد؟ ♪</b>

1501
01:43:45.760 --> 01:43:50.880
♪ My heart melts ♪
♪ My soul crumbles ♪

1502
01:43:51.280 --> 01:43:55.440
<b>♪ Oh, my sky ♪</b>

1503
01:43:57.040 --> 01:44:05.040
<b>♪ The only time I saw you ♪</b>

1504
01:44:05.560 --> 01:44:10.920
♪ In my joy ♪
♪ I was dumbfounded ♪

1505
01:44:11.160 --> 01:44:15.400
<b>♪ At a loss for words ♪</b>

1506
01:44:16.880 --> 01:44:22.160
<b>♪ Before this maiden... ♪</b>

1507
01:44:22.880 --> 01:44:25.760
<b>♪ I melted like snow ♪</b>

1508
01:44:25.800 --> 01:44:31.160
<b>♪ When you're not around ♪</b>

1509
01:44:31.760 --> 01:44:36.400
<b>♪ I am nowhere to be found ♪</b>

1510
01:44:37.280 --> 01:44:41.880
<b>♪ When you're not around ♪</b>

1511
01:44:42.120 --> 01:44:43.880
<b>Your mother's bracelet.</b>

1512
01:44:44.000 --> 01:44:48.760
<b>♪ I am nowhere to be found ♪</b>

1513
01:44:52.560 --> 01:44:55.000
Are you still going to call this
mere friendship, Mathi?

1514
01:44:56.640 --> 01:44:59.520
Don't call this a mere friendship
and lie to yourself.

1515
01:45:00.640 --> 01:45:03.240
I don't know what's the reason
behind your hesitation.

1516
01:45:04.000 --> 01:45:06.160
But I can definitely say
I can't live without you.

1517
01:45:06.440 --> 01:45:08.000
<b>Not even for a second.</b>

1518
01:45:11.520 --> 01:45:12.640
<b>I love you.</b>

1519
01:45:18.680 --> 01:45:20.160
<b>I swear on myself.</b>

1520
01:45:26.160 --> 01:45:28.240
Don't break the promise
under any cost.

1521
01:45:50.280 --> 01:45:52.760
Aslan, the man you are looking for
is called Nellaiappan.

1522
01:45:53.000 --> 01:45:55.520
He is a journalist.
He's been missing for three days now.

1523
01:45:55.640 --> 01:45:59.120
The video you saw in Russia
was shot at the spa in Tulip
Park Hotel.

1524
01:45:59.280 --> 01:46:01.760
Nellai has gone to the hotel several times
to use the spa.

1525
01:46:01.760 --> 01:46:03.880
Nawab was in the hotel
at the same time.

1526
01:46:04.160 --> 01:46:06.240
<b>But we don't have any CCTV footage...</b>

1527
01:46:06.400 --> 01:46:09.760
which shows both of them in the same room
or that they even
met at all.

1528
01:46:09.880 --> 01:46:11.640
I've attached the snaps
from the CCTV.

1529
01:46:11.760 --> 01:46:13.400
<b>So the hacker was right again.</b>

1530
01:46:13.440 --> 01:46:15.280
Nellai is our trump card.
- Yes!

1531
01:46:15.400 --> 01:46:20.400
Check for any calls, messages or transactions
between them
through some closed circle...

1532
01:46:20.520 --> 01:46:23.560
Yes, we did a complete verification,
just like you asked us
to.

1533
01:46:23.760 --> 01:46:27.280
There are no calls, messages, emails
or transactions between
 Nellai and Nawab.

1534
01:46:28.000 --> 01:46:31.640
But we found several calls made between
Nellai and Nawab's
personal driver, Yadav.

1535
01:46:31.680 --> 01:46:32.560
<b>What?</b>

1536
01:46:32.640 --> 01:46:34.560
Well, then get him under
our custody immediately.

1537
01:46:34.640 --> 01:46:36.120
<b>Sir, we tried to contact him.</b>

1538
01:46:36.280 --> 01:46:38.240
<b>But his number is not reachable.</b>

1539
01:46:38.240 --> 01:46:39.400
<b>Great!</b>

1540
01:46:39.440 --> 01:46:41.000
<b>Another missing link.</b>

1541
01:46:42.000 --> 01:46:43.800
Deploy a search team
to find him.

1542
01:46:44.880 --> 01:46:47.760
<b>This guy knows something for sure!</b>

1543
01:47:05.000 --> 01:47:06.040
<b>Hey, Yadav!</b>

1544
01:47:06.120 --> 01:47:08.280
Sir, please, sir.
Let me go.

1545
01:47:08.560 --> 01:47:10.120
<b>Nice view, huh?</b>

1546
01:47:12.160 --> 01:47:13.440
<b>You know what, Yadav?</b>

1547
01:47:13.640 --> 01:47:16.760
This is something important that
humans can learn from
rocket science.

1548
01:47:17.640 --> 01:47:19.240
<b>The further the rocket goes up...</b>

1549
01:47:19.400 --> 01:47:22.400
it will detach the empty fuel tanks
one by one.

1550
01:47:23.560 --> 01:47:24.640
<b>You know why?</b>

1551
01:47:25.520 --> 01:47:27.560
<b>Because it's dead weight, my friend!</b>

1552
01:47:28.640 --> 01:47:29.920
<b>Unnecessary weight.</b>

1553
01:47:30.400 --> 01:47:33.280
When we don't need something anymore,
we must let go of it
immediately.

1554
01:47:34.280 --> 01:47:37.640
And now, you look like
dead weight to me, Yadav!

1555
01:47:37.640 --> 01:47:39.640
<b>Sir, please don't kill me.</b>

1556
01:47:39.800 --> 01:47:41.560
<b>Then prove me wrong, man.</b>

1557
01:47:41.880 --> 01:47:43.120
<b>What use are you to me?</b>

1558
01:47:43.120 --> 01:47:45.400
I saw him, sir. 
I saw him, sir.

1559
01:47:45.520 --> 01:47:47.280
<b>I saw him, sir.</b>

1560
01:47:47.400 --> 01:47:48.880
<b>I saw him, sir.</b>

1561
01:47:49.000 --> 01:47:52.400
I went to Nellai's house
but only his family was there.

1562
01:47:52.440 --> 01:47:54.440
<b>But he abducted Nellai...</b>

1563
01:47:54.520 --> 01:47:56.560
<b>I saw the guy who abducted Nellai.</b>

1564
01:47:56.760 --> 01:47:59.240
<b>I saw the guy who abducted Nellai.</b>

1565
01:47:59.560 --> 01:48:00.800
<b>I have a photo of him.</b>

1566
01:48:00.880 --> 01:48:02.680
I have his photo.
I have his photo, sir.

1567
01:48:02.800 --> 01:48:04.560
<b>I have a photo of him.</b>

1568
01:48:04.640 --> 01:48:05.520
<b>Where?</b>

1569
01:48:05.520 --> 01:48:07.000
My phone.
On my phone, sir.

1570
01:48:07.520 --> 01:48:08.760
<b>Sir...</b>

1571
01:48:21.440 --> 01:48:22.880
<b>Hold still!</b>

1572
01:48:23.920 --> 01:48:25.400
<b>Hold still...</b>

1573
01:48:28.120 --> 01:48:29.240
Where is it?
- Gallery...

1574
01:48:29.400 --> 01:48:31.040
It's the last photo
in the gallery.

1575
01:48:33.000 --> 01:48:34.680
<b>Sir, it hurts so bad.</b>

1576
01:48:34.880 --> 01:48:36.760
<b>Forward this to all our men.</b>

1577
01:48:37.040 --> 01:48:39.560
Tell them to search
every single alley in Kolkata.

1578
01:48:40.040 --> 01:48:41.760
Ten crores for the person
who finds him.

1579
01:48:42.520 --> 01:48:43.640
<b>I need him.</b>

1580
01:48:43.680 --> 01:48:46.120
Sir, please let me go.
It hurts so bad.

1581
01:48:46.400 --> 01:48:47.560
<b>Sir...</b>

1582
01:49:39.440 --> 01:49:41.120
Careful.
- Okay...

1583
01:50:11.000 --> 01:50:12.800
<b>Hurry up.</b>

1584
01:50:14.520 --> 01:50:16.280
He is here.
Hurry up.

1585
01:51:52.640 --> 01:51:55.000
Have the forensic analysts
examined the crime scene yet?

1586
01:51:55.040 --> 01:51:56.760
No, sir. Not yet.
They are on the way.

1587
01:52:06.160 --> 01:52:08.640
Sir, these two girls
are Nellai's daughters.

1588
01:52:08.760 --> 01:52:11.920
Both of them are doing their
higher education in the US.

1589
01:52:13.920 --> 01:52:18.240
Can an ordinary press reporter
give education to his
daughters in the US?

1590
01:52:18.760 --> 01:52:19.800
<b>Is it possible?</b>

1591
01:52:20.120 --> 01:52:21.400
<b>Not possible, sir.</b>

1592
01:52:30.440 --> 01:52:32.640
How many did you say
are there in Nellai's family?

1593
01:52:32.760 --> 01:52:34.040
<b>Six members in total.</b>

1594
01:52:34.240 --> 01:52:35.880
<b>Him, his wife...</b>

1595
01:52:36.000 --> 01:52:38.000
his mother,
his mother-in-law...

1596
01:52:38.120 --> 01:52:39.240
<b>And two girls.</b>

1597
01:52:40.760 --> 01:52:41.760
<b>That's him.</b>

1598
01:52:41.920 --> 01:52:43.000
<b>His wife.</b>

1599
01:52:43.240 --> 01:52:44.400
<b>His mother.</b>

1600
01:52:44.520 --> 01:52:45.640
<b>His mother-in-law.</b>

1601
01:52:46.120 --> 01:52:47.400
<b>His two daughters.</b>

1602
01:52:48.760 --> 01:52:50.160
<b>Then who is this boy?</b>

1603
01:52:53.120 --> 01:52:55.640
<b>No, that isn't his son.</b>

1604
01:52:56.000 --> 01:52:59.120
Fifteen years ago, that kid used to
come to his house
regularly.

1605
01:52:59.160 --> 01:53:01.160
<b>He doesn't come here these days.</b>

1606
01:53:01.520 --> 01:53:03.640
Ask him if he knows
where their house is.

1607
01:53:03.680 --> 01:53:06.120
Go straight, take a left
at the bus stand...

1608
01:53:06.160 --> 01:53:07.680
<b>and ask around for Alipur Home.</b>

1609
01:53:10.760 --> 01:53:11.760
<b>Be careful.</b>

1610
01:53:11.880 --> 01:53:14.000
Don't spread my legs.
The stitches might give away!

1611
01:53:14.120 --> 01:53:16.880
Why are you carrying me
like a worthless sack of onions?

1612
01:53:17.040 --> 01:53:18.160
<b>Careful!</b>

1613
01:53:18.640 --> 01:53:19.520
<b>Sir...</b>

1614
01:53:19.800 --> 01:53:22.880
Just take a good close look
and tell us who he is.

1615
01:53:22.880 --> 01:53:25.440
I am long sighted.
Move it away from me.

1616
01:53:28.560 --> 01:53:29.800
<b>Oh, him...</b>

1617
01:53:31.000 --> 01:53:32.240
<b>Do you know him?</b>

1618
01:53:32.240 --> 01:53:33.280
<b>Yes...</b>

1619
01:53:34.160 --> 01:53:35.880
<b>It's Mathiyazhagan.</b>

1620
01:53:36.640 --> 01:53:38.240
<b>Dinesh, don't run!</b>

1621
01:53:38.760 --> 01:53:39.880
Hello, madam...
- What?

1622
01:53:39.880 --> 01:53:41.880
Stay here.
No one is allowed inside.

1623
01:53:42.240 --> 01:53:43.760
<b>But I'm also a part of the team.</b>

1624
01:53:43.880 --> 01:53:44.880
<b>Ask Aslan.</b>

1625
01:53:44.920 --> 01:53:46.000
No, madam.
I'm sorry.

1626
01:53:46.040 --> 01:53:47.000
<b>Stay here.</b>

1627
01:53:53.800 --> 01:53:56.520
Anand, he is a prime witness.
Move him to our office
immediately.

1628
01:53:56.520 --> 01:53:57.440
<b>Okay, sir.</b>

1629
01:53:57.440 --> 01:53:59.400
Hey, Judy. When did you come?
Why didn't you come in?

1630
01:53:59.440 --> 01:54:01.520
They didn't let me inside.
- Sir, Yadav is dead.

1631
01:54:01.680 --> 01:54:02.800
What?
- Yes, sir.

1632
01:54:02.880 --> 01:54:05.160
They shot him dead
at a construction site.

1633
01:54:05.440 --> 01:54:07.760
His body is shattered.
We've sent it for post-mortem.

1634
01:54:09.800 --> 01:54:10.920
<b>We need to hurry.</b>

1635
01:54:11.120 --> 01:54:13.760
Anand, go to the hospital immediately
and collect his
autopsy reports.

1636
01:54:13.760 --> 01:54:15.120
No one else should
get hold of it.

1637
01:54:15.160 --> 01:54:17.240
No, sir. Let me come with you.
We can send Vishnu...

1638
01:54:17.280 --> 01:54:18.680
<b>Anand, please understand.</b>

1639
01:54:18.760 --> 01:54:20.760
I can't trust anyone else
with this.

1640
01:54:20.760 --> 01:54:22.680
I can only trust you.
Please go.

1641
01:54:23.000 --> 01:54:24.280
Judy, let's go.
Come.

1642
01:54:24.440 --> 01:54:25.640
<b>Where are we going?</b>

1643
01:54:25.880 --> 01:54:28.680
I think I've unearthed the origins
of your genius.

1644
01:54:39.400 --> 01:54:41.880
He is right here.
He is following us.

1645
01:54:42.880 --> 01:54:44.040
<b>Where are you now?</b>

1646
01:54:44.120 --> 01:54:45.160
<b>Howrah Station.</b>

1647
01:54:45.240 --> 01:54:46.520
<b>Don't tell anyone else.</b>

1648
01:54:46.640 --> 01:54:48.760
Come to the market area.
Let's box him in.

1649
01:54:49.240 --> 01:54:50.160
<b>Okay.</b>

1650
01:54:50.520 --> 01:54:52.560
Turn left.
Go to the fish market.

1651
01:54:54.000 --> 01:54:55.240
<b>Brother, take left.</b>

1652
01:55:00.640 --> 01:55:01.760
<b>Mathiyazhagan!</b>

1653
01:55:01.880 --> 01:55:03.160
<b>I know him very well.</b>

1654
01:55:03.400 --> 01:55:05.880
He is not a student
one forgets so easily.

1655
01:55:06.000 --> 01:55:07.240
<b>He was a star!</b>

1656
01:55:07.440 --> 01:55:08.640
<b>A genius.</b>

1657
01:55:08.800 --> 01:55:11.400
The first state rank holder
from our school.

1658
01:55:11.560 --> 01:55:13.640
<b>We can never forget him!</b>

1659
01:55:14.240 --> 01:55:17.040
<b>Sister, this genius of yours...</b>

1660
01:55:17.680 --> 01:55:19.160
<b>how good was he at maths?</b>

1661
01:55:20.160 --> 01:55:21.400
<b>Extraordinary!</b>

1662
01:55:21.880 --> 01:55:25.400
He could solve 12th grade math problems
when he was in grade
 5!

1663
01:55:25.880 --> 01:55:29.520
He's asked me several times why the school
wouldn't teach
more advanced maths.

1664
01:55:29.640 --> 01:55:35.040
The school sponsored him to attend
Olympiads and conferences
 at several countries.

1665
01:55:35.640 --> 01:55:36.680
<b>But you know what?</b>

1666
01:55:36.880 --> 01:55:38.800
<b>He was not just good at maths.</b>

1667
01:55:38.880 --> 01:55:41.520
<b>He was equally good with computers.</b>

1668
01:55:42.000 --> 01:55:45.440
When the other kids used to
play games on the computer...

1669
01:55:45.680 --> 01:55:49.520
even at that young age,
he used to design advanced computer
games.

1670
01:55:53.520 --> 01:55:54.760
<b>Fifteen hours to go!</b>

1671
01:55:56.400 --> 01:55:57.760
<b>Fifteen hours to go!</b>

1672
01:55:59.040 --> 01:56:01.040
<b>Fifteen hours to go!</b>

1673
01:56:11.240 --> 01:56:12.800
<b>I've entered the fish market.</b>

1674
01:56:13.680 --> 01:56:15.040
<b>We are here too.</b>

1675
01:56:16.160 --> 01:56:17.760
<b>Cover the left side.</b>

1676
01:56:18.800 --> 01:56:21.000
Get all our guys on a conference call.
- Okay, boss.

1677
01:56:21.120 --> 01:56:22.680
Yes, brother?
- Hello?

1678
01:56:22.800 --> 01:56:23.880
<b>Hello?</b>

1679
01:56:24.440 --> 01:56:25.560
<b>Where are you?</b>

1680
01:56:31.040 --> 01:56:32.880
<b>Where is he?</b>

1681
01:56:35.160 --> 01:56:36.760
<b>He is right behind me.</b>

1682
01:57:00.440 --> 01:57:01.880
<b>Go this side and look for him.</b>

1683
01:57:01.880 --> 01:57:03.400
<b>You, go there.</b>

1684
01:57:03.880 --> 01:57:06.120
He shouldn't escape.
Search the entire market.

1685
01:57:18.800 --> 01:57:22.040
You think you can beat me up
and escape from here?

1686
01:57:22.880 --> 01:57:26.400
There are thousands of men
like me looking for you in
Kolkata.

1687
01:57:27.800 --> 01:57:29.640
<b>You can't even leave this area!</b>

1688
01:57:30.680 --> 01:57:31.920
<b>Who are you people?</b>

1689
01:57:32.240 --> 01:57:34.400
What did you say about me
over the phone?

1690
01:57:34.880 --> 01:57:36.640
I showed your photo
on the phone and said...

1691
01:57:36.680 --> 01:57:40.400
the guy who kidnapped Nellai
is right here!

1692
01:57:43.120 --> 01:57:46.120
You think you can continue to live
after antagonizing Rishi?

1693
01:57:47.120 --> 01:57:50.120
<b>Just hand Nellai over to us...</b>

1694
01:57:50.400 --> 01:57:53.400
<b>and apologize to Rishi and save your life.</b>

1695
01:57:53.440 --> 01:57:55.120
I saw him.
I just saw him.

1696
01:57:55.240 --> 01:57:57.280
<b>I saw the guy in the photo.</b>

1697
01:57:57.400 --> 01:57:58.680
<b>Are you sure it was him?</b>

1698
01:57:58.760 --> 01:58:01.240
It was him!
He ran into the tram godown.

1699
01:58:01.280 --> 01:58:04.240
Come to the tram godown.
It's the guy from the photo for
sure!

1700
01:58:04.240 --> 01:58:06.040
<b>Everyone, come to the tram godown.</b>

1701
01:58:06.120 --> 01:58:08.160
<b>Please try to understand.</b>

1702
01:58:08.240 --> 01:58:10.880
Aslan, this isn't about maths
or scoring 100 in the exams!

1703
01:58:11.280 --> 01:58:14.440
We are talking about being a prodigy
in two completely
different fields.

1704
01:58:15.000 --> 01:58:17.040
<b>Like, totally genius in it.</b>

1705
01:58:17.520 --> 01:58:19.000
<b>This isn't even possible!</b>

1706
01:58:19.000 --> 01:58:20.160
<b>Just think about it.</b>

1707
01:58:20.520 --> 01:58:25.000
This guy has hacked the servers
at the Interpol Headquarters
 and the CBI.

1708
01:58:25.440 --> 01:58:27.640
He must be a genius
with computers.

1709
01:58:28.000 --> 01:58:30.760
<b>But Cobra is a mathematician for sure!</b>

1710
01:58:31.640 --> 01:58:33.520
What if they are
two different people?

1711
01:58:34.400 --> 01:58:36.640
And maybe there is
some rift between them?

1712
01:58:37.040 --> 01:58:38.680
<b>Shut the gates!</b>

1713
01:58:39.160 --> 01:58:40.640
<b>Lock all the doors.</b>

1714
01:58:51.120 --> 01:58:53.680
I saw him at the tram godown,
but can't find him now.

1715
01:58:53.760 --> 01:58:54.760
<b>We are looking.</b>

1716
01:59:02.000 --> 01:59:03.880
He is near the last tram,
running away.

1717
01:59:04.520 --> 01:59:06.120
<b>Come to the last tram.</b>

1718
02:00:20.800 --> 02:00:22.000
<b>Answer the phone.</b>

1719
02:00:26.880 --> 02:00:28.520
<b>I said, answer the phone.</b>

1720
02:00:35.120 --> 02:00:36.440
<b>Just do as I say.</b>

1721
02:00:37.000 --> 02:00:39.920
No matter what happens here,
you can leave this place alive.

1722
02:00:40.560 --> 02:00:42.000
<b>Why are these people chasing me?</b>

1723
02:00:42.400 --> 02:00:44.560
Who are they?
- He is right here.

1724
02:00:45.000 --> 02:00:46.760
He is on the phone
with someone.

1725
02:00:47.240 --> 02:00:48.400
<b>Look for him.</b>

1726
02:00:48.440 --> 02:00:49.760
<b>Hello, answer me!</b>

1727
02:00:50.880 --> 02:00:52.520
<b>Just listen to me!</b>

1728
02:00:52.560 --> 02:00:53.920
<b>Why should I listen to you?</b>

1729
02:00:54.040 --> 02:00:55.520
<b>Who are you to me?</b>

1730
02:01:07.280 --> 02:01:08.640
<b>Just listen to me!</b>

1731
02:01:09.760 --> 02:01:11.400
Take the right
and get out of here.

1732
02:01:20.760 --> 02:01:22.240
<b>He ran into the market.</b>

1733
02:01:22.280 --> 02:01:24.000
<b>Everyone, go into the market.</b>

1734
02:01:35.520 --> 02:01:37.400
Buy an umbrella from
the shop ahead of you.

1735
02:01:37.440 --> 02:01:38.520
<b>What for?</b>

1736
02:01:38.880 --> 02:01:39.880
<b>Just buy it!</b>

1737
02:01:41.160 --> 02:01:42.240
How much?
- 100 rupees.

1738
02:01:43.240 --> 02:01:45.400
<b>He is buying an umbrella here.</b>

1739
02:01:57.800 --> 02:02:01.040
Box him in from all sides.
Let's see how he escapes from
here!

1740
02:02:01.880 --> 02:02:03.880
Did anyone see the colour
of his umbrella?

1741
02:02:04.000 --> 02:02:06.680
He has a yellow umbrella
with blue stripes. I saw him!

1742
02:02:07.880 --> 02:02:10.000
Don't stop.
Keep walking until I say so.

1743
02:02:14.920 --> 02:02:16.120
<b>Tell me atleast now!</b>

1744
02:02:16.280 --> 02:02:18.160
Who are these people?
Why are they after me?

1745
02:02:18.160 --> 02:02:21.040
Can any of you understand
anything they are saying?

1746
02:02:22.280 --> 02:02:23.280
<b>Tell me...</b>

1747
02:02:23.880 --> 02:02:24.880
<b>Who are these guys?</b>

1748
02:02:24.920 --> 02:02:26.760
They are the goons
of this guy called Rishi.

1749
02:02:27.160 --> 02:02:29.000
<b>Oh, Rishi?</b>

1750
02:02:30.640 --> 02:02:32.120
<b>Has he found me?</b>

1751
02:02:32.440 --> 02:02:33.760
<b>Do you know Rishi?</b>

1752
02:02:35.760 --> 02:02:36.880
<b>Answer me!</b>

1753
02:02:37.520 --> 02:02:38.760
<b>You know Rishi?</b>

1754
02:02:43.400 --> 02:02:45.880
He is on the left side,
near the paan shop.

1755
02:02:50.160 --> 02:02:52.000
<b>He is getting away!</b>

1756
02:03:13.560 --> 02:03:16.520
This isn't him! See if you can spot
the same colour umbrella
 elsewhere.

1757
02:03:20.640 --> 02:03:22.680
We couldn't find
a similar umbrella anywhere else.

1758
02:03:23.120 --> 02:03:26.040
How did you get this umbrella?
Answer me!

1759
02:03:26.120 --> 02:03:30.520
Some guy gave his umbrella to me...
and took mine...

1760
02:03:30.560 --> 02:03:33.000
<b>What colour umbrella did you have?</b>

1761
02:03:33.040 --> 02:03:35.640
<b>It's a red umbrella.</b>

1762
02:03:35.800 --> 02:03:39.000
It's a red umbrella.
Look for a red umbrella!

1763
02:03:43.120 --> 02:03:44.760
Why did you ask me
to swap umbrellas?

1764
02:03:45.520 --> 02:03:46.560
<b>Who are you?</b>

1765
02:03:52.920 --> 02:03:54.280
<b>Just answer my questions.</b>

1766
02:03:55.120 --> 02:03:56.880
<b>Why should Rishi send men to kill you?</b>

1767
02:03:57.000 --> 02:03:58.520
<b>What's your rift with Rishi?</b>

1768
02:03:58.680 --> 02:04:00.000
<b>He doesn't have an option.</b>

1769
02:04:00.440 --> 02:04:03.400
If he doesn't find me and Nellai, 
who I've got with me,
within the next 14 hours...

1770
02:04:03.520 --> 02:04:05.560
Rishi and his entire empire
will go down the ground.

1771
02:04:06.400 --> 02:04:07.520
<b>You've got Nellai with you?</b>

1772
02:04:07.560 --> 02:04:08.880
<b>Capo, they got him!</b>

1773
02:04:09.160 --> 02:04:10.120
<b>Yes, tell me?</b>

1774
02:04:10.160 --> 02:04:12.440
<b>Sir, we trapped him inside the market.</b>

1775
02:04:12.520 --> 02:04:15.000
But someone is coming up with ideas
to save him.

1776
02:04:15.040 --> 02:04:16.760
<b>I think they are partners.</b>

1777
02:04:17.560 --> 02:04:19.440
I don't care if it's two of them
or two thousand.

1778
02:04:19.760 --> 02:04:21.160
<b>I need him alive.</b>

1779
02:04:21.400 --> 02:04:22.400
<b>Get it?</b>

1780
02:04:22.520 --> 02:04:24.000
<b>I need him alive.</b>

1781
02:04:25.040 --> 02:04:27.880
<b>Go back and tell your boss...</b>

1782
02:04:28.120 --> 02:04:30.560
<b>tell Rishi that his time is up.</b>

1783
02:04:30.760 --> 02:04:33.000
<b>No one can silence Nellai now.</b>

1784
02:04:33.280 --> 02:04:35.000
<b>No, don't talk to him!</b>

1785
02:04:35.880 --> 02:04:37.640
Who the hell are you
to call time on Rishi Sir?

1786
02:04:37.880 --> 02:04:40.000
Let me see how you get out
of this market!

1787
02:04:42.000 --> 02:04:44.240
Tell him to add me
to the conference call.

1788
02:04:47.800 --> 02:04:48.880
<b>You are making a mistake.</b>

1789
02:04:49.120 --> 02:04:51.680
Keeping Nellai with you is like
signing your own death
warrant!

1790
02:04:51.760 --> 02:04:52.800
<b>Try to understand.</b>

1791
02:04:52.880 --> 02:04:54.160
<b>Tell me where he is.</b>

1792
02:04:54.280 --> 02:04:56.680
I'll make sure
he doesn't lay a finger on you.

1793
02:04:57.920 --> 02:04:59.120
<b>Dude, seriously?</b>

1794
02:04:59.240 --> 02:05:01.880
Do I look like someone
who is scared of these guys?

1795
02:05:02.000 --> 02:05:04.800
No matter what happens,
I won't reveal Nellai's location.

1796
02:05:04.880 --> 02:05:05.760
<b>Listen to me!</b>

1797
02:05:05.880 --> 02:05:07.880
<b>Shut up and listen to me, Mathi!</b>

1798
02:05:12.400 --> 02:05:13.400
<b>Mathi...</b>

1799
02:05:15.800 --> 02:05:17.800
The name of the hacker
who kidnapped Nellai is...

1800
02:05:18.000 --> 02:05:19.000
<b>Mathi.</b>

1801
02:05:19.120 --> 02:05:20.520
<b>Oh, that?</b>

1802
02:05:21.000 --> 02:05:23.160
He was a loafer,
just like me.

1803
02:05:23.280 --> 02:05:26.640
But after he met a girl called Jenny,
he eloped with her.

1804
02:05:26.760 --> 02:05:27.640
<b>Jenny?</b>

1805
02:05:27.640 --> 02:05:28.920
<b>Yes, Jenny.</b>

1806
02:05:29.040 --> 02:05:30.680
<b>Her family didn't agree to it.</b>

1807
02:05:30.800 --> 02:05:33.160
<b>But her family didn't accept him.</b>

1808
02:05:33.160 --> 02:05:34.560
<b>She was the Commissioner's daughter.</b>

1809
02:05:34.640 --> 02:05:36.240
<b>They even tried beating him up.</b>

1810
02:05:36.400 --> 02:05:39.000
And one fine day,
I heard a loud thud.

1811
02:05:39.400 --> 02:05:40.560
<b>It was an accident.</b>

1812
02:05:40.640 --> 02:05:42.440
<b>We heard the girl had died in it.</b>

1813
02:05:42.520 --> 02:05:45.560
<b>I heard you are scary good at maths!</b>

1814
02:05:47.280 --> 02:05:48.440
<b>Mathi Sir...</b>

1815
02:08:54.400 --> 02:08:55.560
<b>Just wait and watch...</b>

1816
02:08:55.800 --> 02:08:57.880
<b>when you have a problem...</b>

1817
02:08:58.160 --> 02:09:00.160
<b>he will be there for you.</b>

1818
02:09:01.760 --> 02:09:03.680
<b>Sir, I beg you.</b>

1819
02:09:03.880 --> 02:09:06.800
<b>Please don't separate my sons.</b>

1820
02:09:06.920 --> 02:09:08.640
<b>Listen to me, lady.</b>

1821
02:09:08.800 --> 02:09:11.040
The government will put Mathi up
in a good orphanage.

1822
02:09:11.120 --> 02:09:14.240
But we have to send this mad boy
to a psychiatric hospital.

1823
02:09:22.440 --> 02:09:25.040
<b>Sir, please don't call him mad.</b>

1824
02:09:25.120 --> 02:09:26.920
<b>We don't have the time for this!</b>

1825
02:09:27.000 --> 02:09:29.400
Take the mad boy
to the hospital tomorrow.

1826
02:09:31.640 --> 02:09:33.560
<b>Don't call him mad!</b>

1827
02:09:33.640 --> 02:09:35.640
<b>Don't call him mad!</b>

1828
02:09:39.000 --> 02:09:40.680
<b>He has a name.</b>

1829
02:09:41.920 --> 02:09:42.920
<b>Kathir!</b>

1830
02:09:43.440 --> 02:09:44.400
<b>Ma...</b>

1831
02:09:45.520 --> 02:09:46.640
<b>I'll kick you so hard!</b>

1832
02:09:46.680 --> 02:09:49.120
You think you are some big shot
because you bombed some cops
 to death?

1833
02:09:49.120 --> 02:09:50.400
<b>Lucky for you...</b>

1834
02:09:50.440 --> 02:09:53.120
Your mercy petition got rejected,
and you are going to be
hanged tomorrow.

1835
02:09:53.240 --> 02:09:56.640
Or we'd have beaten you to
a painful death inside your cell.

1836
02:09:56.760 --> 02:09:58.440
<b>Sir, he is crossing the limits.</b>

1837
02:09:58.520 --> 02:10:02.920
The whole world knows what the police
do to the women in
their village.

1838
02:10:03.000 --> 02:10:06.880
Are all of you police ganging up and labelling
this
perfectly normal boy as crazy...

1839
02:10:06.920 --> 02:10:08.560
<b>to get back at this woman?</b>

1840
02:10:08.640 --> 02:10:09.800
<b>Perfectly normal boy?</b>

1841
02:10:09.880 --> 02:10:10.880
<b>Look at him!</b>

1842
02:10:10.880 --> 02:10:13.520
He's gone up the tower
and scribbled all over the walls.

1843
02:10:13.560 --> 02:10:15.760
When we ask him a question,
he just does this.

1844
02:10:15.800 --> 02:10:17.040
<b>He talks to himself.</b>

1845
02:10:17.160 --> 02:10:18.760
What else do we call him,
if not mad?

1846
02:10:18.880 --> 02:10:21.520
<b>Sir, I am Kathir's maths teacher.</b>

1847
02:10:21.680 --> 02:10:23.800
He is a born prodigy.
A genius.

1848
02:10:24.000 --> 02:10:27.880
His IQ is much higher than
other kids of his age.

1849
02:10:28.000 --> 02:10:30.000
<b>Please don't call him mad, sir.</b>

1850
02:10:30.120 --> 02:10:32.400
<b>Ma, I don't want him.</b>

1851
02:10:32.560 --> 02:10:34.800
I can't stand watching you
getting beaten up.

1852
02:10:34.880 --> 02:10:36.640
<b>Let him get lost somewhere.</b>

1853
02:10:36.880 --> 02:10:38.000
<b>Let him go!</b>

1854
02:10:38.040 --> 02:10:41.000
<b>What will he do without you?</b>

1855
02:10:41.760 --> 02:10:43.000
<b>Just wait and watch...</b>

1856
02:10:43.040 --> 02:10:45.160
<b>when you have a problem...</b>

1857
02:10:45.560 --> 02:10:47.560
<b>he will be there for you.</b>

1858
02:10:47.800 --> 02:10:49.520
He just doesn't know
how to express his love.

1859
02:10:49.520 --> 02:10:51.160
<b>I hope you aren't angry with me.</b>

1860
02:10:51.640 --> 02:10:53.400
<b>I didn't say that on purpose.</b>

1861
02:10:53.640 --> 02:10:57.040
I said it out of anger
because they hit Ma.

1862
02:10:57.560 --> 02:10:59.000
<b>I know, Mathi.</b>

1863
02:10:59.400 --> 02:11:01.120
<b>How could you ever hate me?</b>

1864
02:11:01.440 --> 02:11:03.040
<b>We share the same blood.</b>

1865
02:11:03.120 --> 02:11:05.400
I will never be angry
with you, little one.

1866
02:11:05.800 --> 02:11:07.040
<b>Look there, Ma!</b>

1867
02:11:07.240 --> 02:11:09.640
<b>Even now, he is talking to himself.</b>

1868
02:11:10.040 --> 02:11:12.160
<b>How will he ever be there for me?</b>

1869
02:11:12.520 --> 02:11:16.000
Ma, please ask them to hang me
right next to you.

1870
02:11:16.280 --> 02:11:17.680
<b>Let me come with you.</b>

1871
02:11:17.760 --> 02:11:20.240
Oh, no.
You shouldn't say such things, Mathi.

1872
02:11:20.640 --> 02:11:22.120
<b>Both of you should be here.</b>

1873
02:11:22.240 --> 02:11:27.240
Both of you will study well and grow up
to become well
respected by everyone.

1874
02:11:59.520 --> 02:12:01.000
<b>Put that witch in there.</b>

1875
02:12:01.040 --> 02:12:04.520
She is not some freedom fighter
to deserve a 21-gun salute!

1876
02:12:11.280 --> 02:12:12.760
<b>Cover her with mud.</b>

1877
02:12:37.120 --> 02:12:38.520
<b>Everything is over.</b>

1878
02:12:38.640 --> 02:12:39.640
<b>Sit!</b>

1879
02:12:39.640 --> 02:12:41.400
<b>Are they going to hang me too?</b>

1880
02:12:41.640 --> 02:12:43.000
<b>I am so scared, Kathir!</b>

1881
02:12:43.040 --> 02:12:44.240
<b>So scared.</b>

1882
02:12:45.400 --> 02:12:48.120
I will never let anything
happen to you, little one.

1883
02:12:48.160 --> 02:12:49.400
<b>You will live.</b>

1884
02:12:49.400 --> 02:12:51.520
And just like Ma wanted,
you will live a good life.

1885
02:12:51.920 --> 02:12:54.400
Listen to me.
It wasn't you who committed the murder.

1886
02:12:54.520 --> 02:12:55.520
<b>It was me.</b>

1887
02:12:57.040 --> 02:12:58.280
<b>Mathi didn't kill.</b>

1888
02:12:58.520 --> 02:12:59.760
<b>It was Kathir.</b>

1889
02:13:00.440 --> 02:13:02.520
No matter how the police
question you, just say...

1890
02:13:02.560 --> 02:13:05.880
"It was Kathir who killed him
but I don't know where he has
gone."

1891
02:13:06.240 --> 02:13:09.520
You've denied him food and water for 20 days 
under the
pretence of an interrogation!

1892
02:13:09.560 --> 02:13:11.120
<b>Mathi isn't going to make it.</b>

1893
02:13:11.160 --> 02:13:13.240
He refuses to tell us 
where his brother Kathir is.

1894
02:13:13.280 --> 02:13:15.520
Doctor, give us a certificate
that he is critical due to
food poisoning.

1895
02:13:15.520 --> 02:13:16.520
<b>We will take care of the rest.</b>

1896
02:13:16.520 --> 02:13:18.680
What nonsense!
Are you even human?

1897
02:13:18.800 --> 02:13:21.000
<b>I'll do anything you ask me for life.</b>

1898
02:13:21.120 --> 02:13:22.640
<b>I need the money now.</b>

1899
02:13:22.800 --> 02:13:24.560
Nothing should happen to my brother.
- Kathir!

1900
02:13:24.640 --> 02:13:26.760
Nothing should happen to my brother.
- Kathir!

1901
02:13:27.000 --> 02:13:29.520
The police will put you up
in an orphanage soon.

1902
02:13:29.520 --> 02:13:31.120
<b>Another new ticket, huh?</b>

1903
02:13:31.400 --> 02:13:33.760
I wonder what antics he did
to end up here!

1904
02:13:33.920 --> 02:13:36.680
After that I will come
and be there with you.

1905
02:13:37.240 --> 02:13:38.440
<b>As Mathi.</b>

1906
02:13:38.800 --> 02:13:40.680
<b>This is the best place for us to hide.</b>

1907
02:13:40.760 --> 02:13:43.880
If someone comes into this room,
one of us can hide here.

1908
02:13:44.120 --> 02:13:46.640
Both of us will live
under the name of Mathi.

1909
02:13:46.880 --> 02:13:49.160
This is Kathir - the sun.
Me.

1910
02:13:49.400 --> 02:13:51.920
And that is Mathi - the moon.
You.

1911
02:13:52.040 --> 02:13:54.520
Monday is your day.
You can step out.

1912
02:13:54.560 --> 02:13:57.400
The next day I will step out
as Mathi.

1913
02:13:57.640 --> 02:14:01.760
Let the world never know
what happened to Kathir.

1914
02:14:02.120 --> 02:14:04.760
No one else should ever 
know about this.

1915
02:14:04.880 --> 02:14:06.240
<b>Swear on me.</b>

1916
02:14:06.680 --> 02:14:08.520
<b>Don't you ever break the promise.</b>

1917
02:14:08.560 --> 02:14:10.240
No, Kathir.
Please listen to me.

1918
02:14:10.520 --> 02:14:12.680
Kathir, don't go.
- Don't break the promise.

1919
02:14:25.040 --> 02:14:26.880
How dare you loiter around
in the jail?

1920
02:14:27.000 --> 02:14:29.760
How dare you go after
the Commissioner's daughter?

1921
02:14:30.160 --> 02:14:32.400
<b>A girl child is a family's property.</b>

1922
02:14:32.640 --> 02:14:33.760
<b>A matter of honour.</b>

1923
02:14:34.160 --> 02:14:36.880
We can't let her go astray
and watch like bystanders.

1924
02:14:36.920 --> 02:14:37.880
<b>I'll kill you!</b>

1925
02:14:38.000 --> 02:14:39.240
<b>Die!</b>

1926
02:14:42.120 --> 02:14:44.800
I heard you have an older brother
called Kathir?

1927
02:14:48.760 --> 02:14:50.640
<b>Who looks exactly like you?</b>

1928
02:14:52.760 --> 02:14:55.640
Ten years ago, he killed a cop
and escaped, right?

1929
02:14:57.880 --> 02:14:59.240
<b>Did you ever see him again?</b>

1930
02:15:02.640 --> 02:15:03.560
<b>Did you?</b>

1931
02:15:08.280 --> 02:15:10.880
<b>The case is still open...</b>

1932
02:15:11.640 --> 02:15:15.440
I've asked them to dust the case file
and look into it.

1933
02:15:15.880 --> 02:15:19.560
You might need to come to the station often
for an enquiry.

1934
02:15:19.640 --> 02:15:20.800
<b>Be prepared.</b>

1935
02:15:22.880 --> 02:15:25.120
<b>Mathi, I am really sorry.</b>

1936
02:15:25.160 --> 02:15:26.880
<b>Did they beat you up real bad?</b>

1937
02:15:26.920 --> 02:15:28.920
<b>I swear, I won't spare them.</b>

1938
02:15:29.000 --> 02:15:30.000
<b>Sorry, Mathi.</b>

1939
02:15:30.040 --> 02:15:31.760
<b>Let's not blow this out of proportion.</b>

1940
02:15:32.680 --> 02:15:36.680
I was only being friendly with you,
but they misunderstood
that.

1941
02:15:37.520 --> 02:15:39.520
<b>I can understand your parents' fear.</b>

1942
02:15:40.040 --> 02:15:43.280
Let's not meet again
or talk to each other.

1943
02:15:53.560 --> 02:15:54.880
<b>I am serious.</b>

1944
02:15:55.760 --> 02:15:58.000
Let's not meet again
or talk to each other.

1945
02:16:01.400 --> 02:16:02.880
<b>You don't get to say that.</b>

1946
02:16:03.000 --> 02:16:04.440
<b>Tell him to say that to me.</b>

1947
02:16:07.240 --> 02:16:08.280
<b>I don't get it.</b>

1948
02:16:12.040 --> 02:16:14.280
<b>You don't get to say that, Kathir.</b>

1949
02:16:14.640 --> 02:16:16.440
Tell Mathi to meet me
and say that to me.

1950
02:16:19.880 --> 02:16:21.640
<b>He broke it!</b>

1951
02:16:22.000 --> 02:16:23.760
<b>He broke it!</b>

1952
02:16:25.240 --> 02:16:28.400
He broke your promise
into a million little pieces.

1953
02:16:31.120 --> 02:16:35.160
You are the first hero in the world
to save the villain's
life!

1954
02:16:54.880 --> 02:16:56.880
<b>Mathi, what the hell have you done?</b>

1955
02:16:58.520 --> 02:17:00.240
<b>They called me to the commissioner's house...</b>

1956
02:17:00.400 --> 02:17:03.520
gave me your photo,
and asked me to kill you!

1957
02:17:05.240 --> 02:17:07.240
You are caught up
in something huge!

1958
02:17:07.640 --> 02:17:09.440
<b>They are not ordinary people.</b>

1959
02:17:09.520 --> 02:17:12.000
Even if not for me,
they will use someone else to kill you.

1960
02:17:12.560 --> 02:17:16.280
Please be honest with me
and tell me the truth....

1961
02:17:16.760 --> 02:17:18.880
If you don't,
things would turn tragic.

1962
02:17:19.400 --> 02:17:20.240
<b>Mathi!</b>

1963
02:17:20.240 --> 02:17:21.160
<b>Mathi!</b>

1964
02:17:21.240 --> 02:17:23.000
<b>Mathi, I'm talking to you...</b>

1965
02:17:24.800 --> 02:17:27.000
This isn't enough.
Get some more cotton and tincture.

1966
02:17:27.120 --> 02:17:28.880
<b>Okay, go and take care of Mathi.</b>

1967
02:17:29.640 --> 02:17:31.040
<b>What happened to Mathi?</b>

1968
02:17:31.120 --> 02:17:33.520
Jennifer's brother beat up Mathi
with some men.

1969
02:17:33.560 --> 02:17:34.760
<b>What are you saying!</b>

1970
02:17:44.880 --> 02:17:46.560
<b>Thanks, you guys should go.</b>

1971
02:17:46.760 --> 02:17:48.400
I can take care of myself.
- Come on! How?

1972
02:17:48.560 --> 02:17:50.560
I'm fine.
I can take care of myself.

1973
02:17:50.640 --> 02:17:51.560
<b>Go.</b>

1974
02:17:51.880 --> 02:17:54.000
We are right here.
Let us know if you need something.

1975
02:17:54.120 --> 02:17:55.040
<b>Okay.</b>

1976
02:17:58.680 --> 02:17:59.760
<b>Careful!</b>

1977
02:17:59.880 --> 02:18:01.880
<b>Did they hit you, little one?</b>

1978
02:18:01.880 --> 02:18:03.640
<b>I'm sorry, Kathir.</b>

1979
02:18:04.760 --> 02:18:06.560
Why are you saying
sorry, little one?

1980
02:18:06.760 --> 02:18:07.800
<b>It was a mistake.</b>

1981
02:18:07.880 --> 02:18:09.440
<b>They thought you were me...</b>

1982
02:18:11.240 --> 02:18:12.520
<b>Did they say anything else?</b>

1983
02:18:13.520 --> 02:18:16.000
<b>Her father dug up our old case details.</b>

1984
02:18:16.680 --> 02:18:17.760
<b>Oh?</b>

1985
02:18:17.880 --> 02:18:19.240
<b>Is he threatening us?</b>

1986
02:18:19.240 --> 02:18:20.440
<b>What did he say?</b>

1987
02:18:20.640 --> 02:18:22.240
<b>That he'd put me on a noose?</b>

1988
02:18:22.440 --> 02:18:24.880
They can never separate us,
no matter how hard they try.

1989
02:18:25.760 --> 02:18:28.440
<b>Little one, have you thought this through?</b>

1990
02:18:29.240 --> 02:18:31.240
Do you really need the girl
after all of this?

1991
02:18:31.880 --> 02:18:33.120
<b>You don't need her.</b>

1992
02:18:34.920 --> 02:18:37.640
<b>Kathir, this isn't just some girl.</b>

1993
02:18:37.880 --> 02:18:39.240
<b>She is my angel.</b>

1994
02:18:40.640 --> 02:18:42.640
<b>Not everyone ends up with an angel.</b>

1995
02:18:42.800 --> 02:18:44.800
Have you ever seen me smile
in all these years?

1996
02:18:46.000 --> 02:18:47.760
<b>But I smile these days.</b>

1997
02:18:48.120 --> 02:18:49.880
<b>I finally know what happiness means.</b>

1998
02:18:51.000 --> 02:18:53.240
I feel like I've regained everything
I lost in life.

1999
02:18:54.280 --> 02:18:56.240
<b>I feel like I've got Ma back.</b>

2000
02:18:57.760 --> 02:18:59.640
<b>Not everyone can become Ma, little one.</b>

2001
02:19:01.160 --> 02:19:03.160
<b>The girl doesn't have patience.</b>

2002
02:19:03.560 --> 02:19:05.520
<b>Do you know what she told her father?</b>

2003
02:19:06.120 --> 02:19:08.680
<b>She will lead us to big trouble, little one.</b>

2004
02:19:10.000 --> 02:19:11.160
<b>Are you scared?</b>

2005
02:19:11.400 --> 02:19:14.000
Are you scared our secret will be exposed
and we'd get
caught?

2006
02:19:15.880 --> 02:19:17.760
<b>I won't get you into trouble.</b>

2007
02:19:18.520 --> 02:19:21.680
I am going to leave the city with her
in a few days.

2008
02:19:22.160 --> 02:19:23.560
<b>You can be Mathi all the time.</b>

2009
02:19:23.760 --> 02:19:25.280
<b>Are you going to leave me, little one?</b>

2010
02:19:27.680 --> 02:19:29.880
Has she become more important
to you than me?

2011
02:19:33.920 --> 02:19:34.880
<b>Fine...</b>

2012
02:19:35.400 --> 02:19:36.520
<b>Where will you go?</b>

2013
02:19:36.520 --> 02:19:38.280
<b>Those aren't ordinary guys.</b>

2014
02:19:38.560 --> 02:19:40.400
They will hunt you down
and kill you.

2015
02:19:40.520 --> 02:19:42.520
<b>I just want to be with my Jenny.</b>

2016
02:19:43.400 --> 02:19:45.400
<b>I am ready to sacrifice my life for it.</b>

2017
02:19:46.440 --> 02:19:49.240
<b>You'd sacrifice your life for her?</b>

2018
02:19:51.120 --> 02:19:55.520
As long as I am alive, I won't allow
a single scratch on
your body.

2019
02:19:56.240 --> 02:19:58.640
I'd go to any extent
to protect you.

2020
02:19:58.760 --> 02:20:01.040
If killing the girl is what
it would take to save you...

2021
02:20:02.240 --> 02:20:03.760
<b>I am ready for that too.</b>

2022
02:20:10.640 --> 02:20:12.400
<b>If you dare say another word...</b>

2023
02:20:12.920 --> 02:20:14.240
<b>I'd put an end to you.</b>

2024
02:20:17.120 --> 02:20:18.400
<b>You'd kill her?</b>

2025
02:20:19.120 --> 02:20:21.280
<b>If you even think about it again...</b>

2026
02:20:21.640 --> 02:20:22.880
<b>I'll kill you.</b>

2027
02:21:07.520 --> 02:21:08.800
Jenny?
- Mathi...

2028
02:21:09.000 --> 02:21:10.280
Mathi...
- Jenny?

2029
02:21:10.440 --> 02:21:12.800
Someone is chasing me.
- What are you saying?

2030
02:21:12.880 --> 02:21:14.520
<b>They are chasing me.</b>

2031
02:21:14.640 --> 02:21:15.640
Mathi...
- Who?

2032
02:21:15.760 --> 02:21:16.880
<b>Where are you?</b>

2033
02:21:17.120 --> 02:21:18.280
<b>Who?</b>

2034
02:21:18.680 --> 02:21:19.760
<b>Jenny...</b>

2035
02:21:20.560 --> 02:21:21.680
<b>Kathir!</b>

2036
02:21:21.920 --> 02:21:22.880
<b>Jenny?</b>

2037
02:21:25.000 --> 02:21:26.120
<b>What?</b>

2038
02:21:27.560 --> 02:21:28.520
<b>Jenny?</b>

2039
02:22:05.760 --> 02:22:06.760
<b>Jenny...</b>

2040
02:22:07.120 --> 02:22:08.240
<b>Jenny!</b>

2041
02:22:11.240 --> 02:22:12.240
<b>Mathi...</b>

2042
02:22:17.680 --> 02:22:18.880
<b>Mathi...</b>

2043
02:22:22.000 --> 02:22:23.120
<b>Mathi...</b>

2044
02:22:26.640 --> 02:22:27.640
<b>Mathi!</b>

2045
02:22:32.160 --> 02:22:34.400
Mathi, I am scared.
You should--

2046
02:23:42.400 --> 02:23:43.640
<b>Mathi...</b>

2047
02:23:44.000 --> 02:23:45.880
<b>Mathi, please hear me out.</b>

2048
02:23:46.040 --> 02:23:48.120
Mathi...
- Who is Mathi?

2049
02:23:49.880 --> 02:23:50.880
<b>Me?</b>

2050
02:23:51.800 --> 02:23:53.040
<b>But you are Mathi, aren't you?</b>

2051
02:23:54.440 --> 02:23:56.120
<b>Isn't that why you killed her?</b>

2052
02:23:59.760 --> 02:24:01.680
<b>Are you puzzled how I made it out alive...</b>

2053
02:24:01.760 --> 02:24:04.640
after you threw me into the ship
to rot with the filth in
the ocean?

2054
02:24:06.400 --> 02:24:09.760
I am destined to be the reason
why you get caught and
eventually die.

2055
02:24:11.160 --> 02:24:13.160
<b>That's why God saved me.</b>

2056
02:24:16.120 --> 02:24:18.040
<b>The ship that you threw me in...</b>

2057
02:24:18.560 --> 02:24:22.240
it crossed borders and got caught
by the Thailand coast
guards.

2058
02:24:25.880 --> 02:24:28.520
<b>I was in jail for 10 years.</b>

2059
02:24:29.120 --> 02:24:30.160
<b>It was hell.</b>

2060
02:24:30.920 --> 02:24:32.520
<b>I escaped from the jail in Thailand.</b>

2061
02:24:32.520 --> 02:24:34.000
<b>I was scared to go anywhere.</b>

2062
02:24:34.440 --> 02:24:36.280
I was scared that
someone would identify me.

2063
02:24:36.400 --> 02:24:37.440
<b>But above all...</b>

2064
02:24:37.520 --> 02:24:41.560
I was filled with rage to find you after you escaped
from
Kolkata without leaving any trail behind.

2065
02:24:43.440 --> 02:24:46.680
I installed cameras
in all the places frequented by Nellai.

2066
02:24:47.240 --> 02:24:49.240
<b>I tapped his phone.</b>

2067
02:24:50.640 --> 02:24:54.400
I watched every single move of his
and passed that
information to Interpol.

2068
02:24:54.520 --> 02:24:56.680
I was hoping atleast
they'd be able to catch you...

2069
02:24:56.880 --> 02:24:58.280
<b>but you always got away.</b>

2070
02:24:58.440 --> 02:25:03.400
I went mad trying to
crack your Su-Do-Ku code.

2071
02:25:05.120 --> 02:25:06.520
<b>Then I kidnapped Nellai.</b>

2072
02:25:07.520 --> 02:25:13.240
And I used him to send you
the Su-Do-Ku code I wanted.

2073
02:25:16.880 --> 02:25:20.040
You walked right into it,
like a rat into a trap!

2074
02:25:23.120 --> 02:25:24.760
<b>That moment...</b>

2075
02:25:24.800 --> 02:25:26.800
<b>I was so happy.</b>

2076
02:25:29.760 --> 02:25:32.240
When I admitted you here,
they asked for your details.

2077
02:25:32.920 --> 02:25:34.240
<b>I said I didn't know.</b>

2078
02:25:34.920 --> 02:25:37.440
They said they'd have to inform
the police, as per
procedure.

2079
02:25:38.000 --> 02:25:39.520
<b>I said okay.</b>

2080
02:25:40.920 --> 02:25:44.760
I heard the police know the assassin
who killed people
across the world is you...

2081
02:25:45.800 --> 02:25:49.880
I mean the police know it's Mathi, and they are
looking for
you everywhere to arrest you.

2082
02:25:49.920 --> 02:25:52.040
No, Mathi.
Listen to me...

2083
02:25:52.280 --> 02:25:54.040
<b>You wanted to be Mathi, didn't you?</b>

2084
02:25:55.400 --> 02:25:56.640
<b>So be Mathi!</b>

2085
02:25:57.240 --> 02:25:58.400
<b>No, Mathi.</b>

2086
02:26:00.400 --> 02:26:03.280
Sir, the accused we were looking for
is in the hospital.

2087
02:26:03.400 --> 02:26:05.400
I'll arrest him
and bring him immediately.

2088
02:26:05.880 --> 02:26:07.560
<b>Sir, we have arrested him.</b>

2089
02:26:07.640 --> 02:26:09.240
<b>We will reach in half an hour.</b>

2090
02:26:09.400 --> 02:26:11.000
There is no need
for additional forces, sir.

2091
02:26:11.160 --> 02:26:13.120
Don't worry, sir.
We are on our way.

2092
02:26:34.240 --> 02:26:36.040
<b>How did the press get here?</b>

2093
02:26:37.400 --> 02:26:40.000
Hello, sir? I've sent you a photo.
Please take a look
immediately.

2094
02:26:40.040 --> 02:26:41.920
His name is Mathiyazhagan.
He is a maths teacher.

2095
02:26:42.000 --> 02:26:44.120
I've been following
Aslan's investigation thoroughly.

2096
02:26:44.160 --> 02:26:47.000
I am 100 percent sure
he is the assassin who worked for you.

2097
02:26:52.880 --> 02:26:54.520
Show him the photo
we got from Yadav.

2098
02:27:03.440 --> 02:27:05.240
<b>They are not just two people.</b>

2099
02:27:05.520 --> 02:27:07.400
<b>They are two identical looking people.</b>

2100
02:27:11.560 --> 02:27:13.640
<b>I don't care who Mathiyazhagan is.</b>

2101
02:27:14.120 --> 02:27:16.760
<b>I don't want Aslan to investigate him.</b>

2102
02:27:17.920 --> 02:27:20.120
I'm coming over.
- Sir, let me take care of it!

2103
02:27:20.560 --> 02:27:23.120
I'll try to somehow shift him out
of this case by tonight.

2104
02:27:23.240 --> 02:27:24.520
<b>I'll keep you informed.</b>

2105
02:27:24.640 --> 02:27:25.640
<b>Anand...</b>

2106
02:27:26.400 --> 02:27:28.120
<b>If something goes wrong...</b>

2107
02:27:28.120 --> 02:27:34.240
I will make sure there is no evidence
of a person called
Anand having existed on this earth.

2108
02:27:34.400 --> 02:27:36.240
Sir, I assure you he won't
open his mouth.

2109
02:27:36.240 --> 02:27:37.240
<b>I'll take care of it.</b>

2110
02:27:37.760 --> 02:27:41.680
But I need you to talk to the Home Minister
to grant me full
 control of this case.

2111
02:27:41.880 --> 02:27:43.640
I'll take care of it.
I'll call you back.

2112
02:27:45.040 --> 02:27:46.120
<b>Lift him up!</b>

2113
02:27:46.800 --> 02:27:48.760
<b>Thought you could mess with us?</b>

2114
02:27:59.000 --> 02:28:01.400
What do you mean 'duty'?
- Answer me, sir.

2115
02:28:01.520 --> 02:28:02.560
<b>Sister...</b>

2116
02:28:02.920 --> 02:28:05.160
There is no way anything they said
is true at all.

2117
02:28:06.040 --> 02:28:07.040
<b>Let me go.</b>

2118
02:28:07.400 --> 02:28:08.680
<b>I'll come back with him.</b>

2119
02:28:13.800 --> 02:28:15.560
<b>I don't find it right, general.</b>

2120
02:28:15.560 --> 02:28:17.240
<b>I've been observing certain things here.</b>

2121
02:28:17.240 --> 02:28:18.400
<b>The evidences were tampered.</b>

2122
02:28:18.520 --> 02:28:21.280
And I am damn sure
Rishi is behind this.

2123
02:28:21.280 --> 02:28:23.680
We need to get the custody of Mathiyazhagan
as soon as
possible.

2124
02:28:23.760 --> 02:28:26.000
Or all our hard work
will go to waste.

2125
02:28:27.000 --> 02:28:29.000
<b>Thought you could mess with us?</b>

2126
02:28:31.520 --> 02:28:32.520
<b>Ma'am...</b>

2127
02:28:32.760 --> 02:28:34.000
<b>You've made a mistake, Judy.</b>

2128
02:28:34.440 --> 02:28:35.800
<b>A big big mistake.</b>

2129
02:28:36.440 --> 02:28:39.000
No, ma'am.
I've done you a favour.

2130
02:28:39.240 --> 02:28:41.640
I might be a big fan
of his mathematics.

2131
02:28:41.760 --> 02:28:43.240
But what he committed
was a big crime.

2132
02:28:43.400 --> 02:28:45.000
He will never be able to
get away with it.

2133
02:28:45.120 --> 02:28:46.280
<b>Think about it, ma'am...</b>

2134
02:28:46.400 --> 02:28:47.880
<b>I've done you a favour.</b>

2135
02:28:50.000 --> 02:28:51.000
<b>Ma'am...</b>

2136
02:28:57.120 --> 02:28:59.400
I'm not hitting you
to get you to talk.

2137
02:28:59.880 --> 02:29:02.800
I am hitting you
so you never talk at all.

2138
02:29:03.880 --> 02:29:05.680
<b>If you open your mouth...</b>

2139
02:29:06.640 --> 02:29:08.760
the guy outside who looks
exactly like you...

2140
02:29:09.440 --> 02:29:12.400
he will die in a more brutal way
than you can ever imagine.

2141
02:29:13.640 --> 02:29:16.520
<b>Rishi is watching everything.</b>

2142
02:29:18.560 --> 02:29:19.560
<b>What?</b>

2143
02:29:20.560 --> 02:29:21.880
<b>Do you understand?</b>

2144
02:29:37.240 --> 02:29:38.520
<b>How dare you laugh!</b>

2145
02:29:38.560 --> 02:29:40.880
<b>Don't mess with me, you rascal!</b>

2146
02:29:42.880 --> 02:29:44.520
<b>Do you even call this an investigation?</b>

2147
02:29:44.520 --> 02:29:45.760
<b>What are you even doing?</b>

2148
02:29:45.760 --> 02:29:48.640
You will have to handover the suspect
to me within three
days.

2149
02:29:48.760 --> 02:29:51.880
If something happens to him,
I'll take this to the
international court.

2150
02:29:53.560 --> 02:29:54.520
<b>Vishnu...</b>

2151
02:29:54.880 --> 02:29:56.280
Tell Anand to come here.
- Sure, sir.

2152
02:30:02.280 --> 02:30:03.440
<b>Anand, stop this.</b>

2153
02:30:03.440 --> 02:30:04.680
<b>Lower him immediately.</b>

2154
02:30:04.760 --> 02:30:05.680
<b>What?</b>

2155
02:30:06.280 --> 02:30:08.120
<b>Why should I stop questioning him?</b>

2156
02:30:08.560 --> 02:30:10.880
If you want him to talk within a day,
this is the only way.

2157
02:30:10.920 --> 02:30:12.760
Is that so, sir?
By gagging him?

2158
02:30:12.760 --> 02:30:14.680
You expect him to
talk through his ears?

2159
02:30:16.280 --> 02:30:19.120
Anand, I can definitely sense
something wrong with you.

2160
02:30:19.240 --> 02:30:21.240
Oh?
Nice!

2161
02:30:21.240 --> 02:30:24.400
Stop it! Bring him down and get him
to the interrogation
room.

2162
02:31:08.560 --> 02:31:11.400
You haven't even allowed me to use
the bathroom, like I'm
some criminal.

2163
02:31:11.440 --> 02:31:12.760
<b>This is torture, sir.</b>

2164
02:31:12.760 --> 02:31:14.280
We got engaged yesterday.
- You live with him, right?

2165
02:31:14.400 --> 02:31:16.000
We were supposed to
get married today.

2166
02:31:16.000 --> 02:31:17.400
<b>Why didn't the wedding happen?</b>

2167
02:31:17.400 --> 02:31:18.760
<b>I have already answered that.</b>

2168
02:31:18.760 --> 02:31:21.520
You need to answer it
every time we ask you, madam.

2169
02:31:21.880 --> 02:31:24.640
<b>I will answer if you ask me respectfully.</b>

2170
02:31:24.640 --> 02:31:26.640
<b>Just answer the damn question!</b>

2171
02:31:26.880 --> 02:31:31.680
You were about to marry a criminal
without knowing his
background....

2172
02:31:31.760 --> 02:31:33.040
<b>you don't deserve any respect!</b>

2173
02:31:33.120 --> 02:31:36.760
Why should he raise someone like you,
who was born to a
ganja peddler and an immoral woman?

2174
02:31:36.880 --> 02:31:38.680
Cut the act and stop crying.
Answer me.

2175
02:31:38.760 --> 02:31:40.800
You live in the house, don't you?
- Please let me go.

2176
02:31:46.440 --> 02:31:48.640
What would be running inside
that genius brain of his?

2177
02:31:53.240 --> 02:31:54.920
Your time is running out
way too fast.

2178
02:31:55.160 --> 02:31:56.800
Things are going to get
even worse for you.

2179
02:31:59.400 --> 02:32:00.680
<b>What wrong did they do?</b>

2180
02:32:00.760 --> 02:32:02.120
<b>Why should they suffer?</b>

2181
02:32:02.280 --> 02:32:03.520
<b>What is wrong with you?</b>

2182
02:32:03.760 --> 02:32:05.240
<b>What the hell is wrong with you?</b>

2183
02:32:22.560 --> 02:32:23.880
<b>He is the real problem.</b>

2184
02:32:24.240 --> 02:32:26.000
<b>This little punk is our problem.</b>

2185
02:32:26.240 --> 02:32:28.240
<b>Blood is thicker than water.</b>

2186
02:32:28.280 --> 02:32:29.920
<b>That's the real matter.</b>

2187
02:32:30.680 --> 02:32:31.640
<b>Emotion.</b>

2188
02:32:32.000 --> 02:32:33.120
<b>Affection.</b>

2189
02:32:33.880 --> 02:32:35.520
<b>Gopal...</b>

2190
02:32:38.240 --> 02:32:39.640
Lose it, man.
Lose it.

2191
02:32:39.640 --> 02:32:40.760
<b>Get lost, you loser!</b>

2192
02:32:40.800 --> 02:32:42.240
<b>Emotions have no value.</b>

2193
02:32:42.520 --> 02:32:44.920
They are neither scalar nor vector
nor can be measured!

2194
02:32:46.000 --> 02:32:48.440
The only difference between
a genius and a fool is...

2195
02:32:49.400 --> 02:32:51.120
<b>emotional decisions.</b>

2196
02:32:52.800 --> 02:32:56.680
Teacher, it doesn't matter if you
talk in length in a husky
voice...

2197
02:32:56.800 --> 02:32:58.400
<b>or if you swear at him!</b>

2198
02:32:58.640 --> 02:33:00.240
Nothing will get past
his thick skull!

2199
02:33:02.000 --> 02:33:03.440
<b>There he goes again!</b>

2200
02:33:07.280 --> 02:33:09.120
<b>Yes, that is how my son is.</b>

2201
02:33:09.240 --> 02:33:10.560
<b>I raised him that way.</b>

2202
02:33:10.880 --> 02:33:13.000
If Mathi is in trouble,
he will be there for him.

2203
02:33:13.760 --> 02:33:15.400
<b>All of you have changed him.</b>

2204
02:33:15.520 --> 02:33:16.880
Oh yes,
we changed him.

2205
02:33:16.920 --> 02:33:19.120
It was us,
we changed him!

2206
02:33:19.160 --> 02:33:21.520
We changed him, we changed him,
we changed him.

2207
02:33:21.520 --> 02:33:23.760
We changed him, we changed him,
we changed him.

2208
02:33:48.400 --> 02:33:49.520
<b>What the hell!</b>

2209
02:33:49.640 --> 02:33:51.440
<b>Why are you feeling sorry for her?</b>

2210
02:33:51.640 --> 02:33:53.800
She is responsible for everything
that happened to you.

2211
02:33:53.920 --> 02:33:55.000
<b>She deserved to die.</b>

2212
02:33:55.120 --> 02:33:57.120
It is not your fault
that she died.

2213
02:33:58.400 --> 02:33:59.520
<b>Grab the stick!</b>

2214
02:34:00.640 --> 02:34:02.880
Oh, yes.
It wasn't his fault.

2215
02:34:03.120 --> 02:34:05.400
<b>Then why is she chasing him?</b>

2216
02:34:05.560 --> 02:34:07.400
<b>Why is she taking revenge on him?</b>

2217
02:34:09.160 --> 02:34:10.640
<b>Exactly the point!</b>

2218
02:34:10.680 --> 02:34:12.240
<b>He is being a showoff, My Lord!</b>

2219
02:34:13.400 --> 02:34:14.520
<b>Kill him!</b>

2220
02:34:14.760 --> 02:34:15.880
<b>You can do it.</b>

2221
02:34:15.920 --> 02:34:17.240
<b>Even at this moment...</b>

2222
02:34:17.400 --> 02:34:22.000
you are a freaking genius with numbers
in every goddamn cell
 of your body.

2223
02:34:23.160 --> 02:34:24.280
<b>Who?</b>

2224
02:34:27.640 --> 02:34:29.880
If you speak up and confess,
we can atleast save them.

2225
02:34:30.280 --> 02:34:31.760
<b>Are you going to speak up or not?</b>

2226
02:34:34.400 --> 02:34:36.120
How much longer
are you going to remain silent?

2227
02:34:36.160 --> 02:34:37.520
<b>What do we look like to you?</b>

2228
02:34:38.280 --> 02:34:39.680
<b>You look like losers!</b>

2229
02:34:40.640 --> 02:34:42.400
<b>Go for it, Kathir!</b>

2230
02:34:42.640 --> 02:34:44.880
You know what they'd do
to Mathi if they catch him.

2231
02:34:44.920 --> 02:34:46.920
<b>Rishi will kill Mathi anyway.</b>

2232
02:34:47.120 --> 02:34:49.640
What's the point
if both Mathi and you die?

2233
02:34:49.680 --> 02:34:52.040
You know how to save yourself
with minimal loss.

2234
02:34:52.760 --> 02:34:54.000
<b>Game theory!</b>

2235
02:34:54.640 --> 02:34:55.920
<b>Just apply it!</b>

2236
02:34:56.120 --> 02:34:57.760
<b>To hell with your apples.</b>

2237
02:34:57.800 --> 02:34:59.640
Go away, he isn't going to
listen to you.

2238
02:34:59.680 --> 02:35:01.120
<b>You shut up!</b>

2239
02:35:01.160 --> 02:35:03.040
<b>Kathir, please listen to me.</b>

2240
02:35:03.120 --> 02:35:06.640
Mathematics is not for fools like you.
Don't keep saying the
 same thing.

2241
02:35:06.680 --> 02:35:09.280
He isn't going to listen to you.
Just shut the crap.

2242
02:35:09.400 --> 02:35:11.640
<b>Shut up, man.</b>

2243
02:35:11.680 --> 02:35:12.880
<b>Shut up, man</b>

2244
02:35:13.000 --> 02:35:14.760
Won't you listen to me?
- Genius...

2245
02:35:14.800 --> 02:35:16.000
<b>Be quiet, all of you.</b>

2246
02:35:16.000 --> 02:35:18.240
Not a word of what he says
should go into your brain.

2247
02:35:18.400 --> 02:35:19.800
<b>This is absolute shit!</b>

2248
02:35:19.920 --> 02:35:21.240
<b>Shut up and listen to me.</b>

2249
02:35:28.880 --> 02:35:30.120
<b>Open your mouth and speak up!</b>

2250
02:35:30.160 --> 02:35:32.520
We know you did all of it.
Just confess.

2251
02:35:48.000 --> 02:35:51.400
گەورەم، داوام لێ دەکەیت دان بە تاوانی کەسێکی تردا بنێم!

2252
02:35:54.880 --> 02:35:56.400
<b>وەستە، چی دەڵێیت؟</b>

2253
02:35:57.000 --> 02:35:58.120
<b>تۆ ماتھی نیت؟</b>

2254
02:35:58.280 --> 02:35:59.280
<b>مامۆستای بیرکاری؟</b>

2255
02:35:59.400 --> 02:36:00.760
<b>گەورەم، من ماتھیـم.</b>

2256
02:36:01.240 --> 02:36:02.640
<b>من مامۆستای بیرکاریشم.</b>

2257
02:36:03.040 --> 02:36:04.560
<b>بەڵام من ئەوەم نەکردووە.</b>

2258
02:36:04.640 --> 02:36:06.520
من ہیچ پەیوەندییەکی
بەم شتانەوە نییە!

2259
02:36:08.400 --> 02:36:10.040
<b>گەورەم، برای گەورەم ھەیە.</b>

2260
02:36:10.400 --> 02:36:11.560
<b>کاتیر.</b>

2261
02:36:14.000 --> 02:36:16.000
<b>ئەمە چی چیرۆکێکی نوێیە؟</b>

2262
02:36:16.120 --> 02:36:20.760
گەورەم، تۆمارەکانی زیندانی کۆلکتا
بپشکنە بۆ ساڵی ١٩٨٥.

2263
02:36:28.880 --> 02:36:30.040
<b>تۆمارەکانی زیندان بپشکنە.</b>

2264
02:36:30.120 --> 02:36:31.760
دەستبەجێ دڵنیابەرەوە
و پێم بڵێوە.

2265
02:36:31.800 --> 02:36:33.000
<b>خێرا بکە!</b>

2266
02:36:39.400 --> 02:36:40.640
<b>گەورەم، ئەوان دوو کەسن.</b>

2267
02:36:40.760 --> 02:36:42.120
<b>کاتیڤێلان و ماتییازھاگان.</b>

2268
02:36:42.120 --> 02:36:43.880
ڕاپورتە فەرمییەکان
لە ڕێگان، گەورەم.

2269
02:36:45.520 --> 02:36:47.640
<b>من تەنها خوێندکارێکی ئاساییم، گەورەم.</b>

2270
02:36:48.440 --> 02:36:50.120
<b>بەڵام ئەو زیرەکە.</b>

2271
02:36:50.520 --> 02:36:52.240
<b>ئەو زۆر جیاوازە، گەورەم.</b>

2272
02:36:52.280 --> 02:36:53.920
<b>قسە لەگەڵ کەسدا ناکات، گەورەم.</b>

2273
02:36:54.040 --> 02:36:57.800
لە ساڵی ١٩٩٢، دکتۆر شیتال
پزیشکی مێردمنداڵان بوو.

2274
02:36:57.880 --> 02:36:59.800
<b>دکتۆر شیتال دەزانێت.</b>

2275
02:37:00.280 --> 02:37:01.520
<b>ئەو زۆر باش دەیناسێت.</b>

2276
02:37:01.880 --> 02:37:03.000
<b>ئەو دەروونییە...</b>

2277
02:37:03.520 --> 02:37:05.000
خێرا بکە.
- باشە، گەورەم.

2278
02:37:07.760 --> 02:37:09.400
کاتیر؟
بیرم دێتەوە.

2279
02:37:09.560 --> 02:37:11.040
<b>ئەو منداڵێکی تایبەت بوو.</b>

2280
02:37:11.240 --> 02:37:12.640
<b>بەهرەمەندێکی بیرکاری.</b>

2281
02:37:12.800 --> 02:37:16.160
لە کاتی ڕێوڕەسمی کۆتایی دایکماندا،
پۆلیسێک زۆر بە نایاسایی
ڕەفتاری کرد.

2282
02:37:16.760 --> 02:37:18.040
<b>دێباشیش چاتێرجی.</b>

2283
02:37:18.400 --> 02:37:19.640
<b>لە هەمان شوێن کوشتی.</b>

2284
02:37:20.280 --> 02:37:21.240
<b>کوشتی!</b>

2285
02:37:25.680 --> 02:37:26.800
<b>ئەم پیاوەی ناوی نێلایە...</b>

2286
02:37:26.920 --> 02:37:29.760
سەڕەڕای ئەوەی تەواو نەناسیاوبووم،
ئەوی دەیویست فێرم بکات.

2287
02:37:30.520 --> 02:37:33.640
بۆیە بە خۆشحاڵییەوە گوێم لە هەموو قسەکانی گرت
و دەستمدابە
چوونە قوتابخانە.

2288
02:37:34.400 --> 02:37:39.240
پاش چەند مانگێک بۆم دەرکەوت
کە ئەو و کاتیر
کاری نیاساویان دەکرد.

2289
02:37:39.560 --> 02:37:43.560
و ئەوەی کە ئەوان منیان وەک پەردەیەک بەکاردەهێنا
لە ئەگەری تێکچوونی
کارە نیاساییەکانیان.

2290
02:38:02.880 --> 02:38:04.800
شەوی ڕابردوو هاتە
نەخۆشخانە بۆ بینینم.

2291
02:38:04.880 --> 02:38:07.880
ئەو کاتە بوو کە بۆم دەرکەوت
ئەو منی خستووەتە ناو ئەم
گێژاوە گەورەیەوە.

2292
02:38:08.240 --> 02:38:10.160
<b>من تەنها مامۆستایەکی ئاسایی بیرکاریم.</b>

2293
02:38:11.640 --> 02:38:12.400
<b>گەورەم!</b>

2294
02:38:12.440 --> 02:38:15.000
گەورەم، من تەنها
مامۆستایەکی ئاسایی بیرکاریم.

2295
02:38:15.040 --> 02:38:17.400
گەورەم، من هیچ پەیوەندییەکی
بەو شتانەوە نییە.

2296
02:38:17.560 --> 02:38:18.880
<b>گەورەم، تکایە...</b>

2297
02:38:19.000 --> 02:38:20.240
براکەم!
سڵاو؟

2298
02:38:23.640 --> 02:38:24.800
<b>گەورەم...</b>

2299
02:38:32.120 --> 02:38:34.280
گەورەم، ئێستا چی بکەین؟
- ئەو کێشەی ئێمە نییە، ئاناند.

2300
02:38:34.880 --> 02:38:36.760
ئەو هاککەرەی دەرەوەیە
کە کێشەی ئێمەیە.

2301
02:38:45.680 --> 02:38:46.640
<b>وەستە!</b>

2302
02:38:48.880 --> 02:38:51.920
کەواتە ئەوە ئەو پیاوەیە
کە هەموو ئەم ماوەیە یارمەتی دەداین.

2303
02:38:52.520 --> 02:38:55.120
ئەو کەسەی کە ماتھی بەستەوە
و وای لێکرد خۆی ڕادەستی
پۆلیس بکات.

2304
02:38:56.760 --> 02:38:57.880
<b>بەڵام خەمی نەبێت.</b>

2305
02:38:58.240 --> 02:38:59.560
<b>پێویست ناکات هیچ بکەین.</b>

2306
02:38:59.800 --> 02:39:01.640
پیاوی بیرکاری تا ئێستا
حیساباتەکەی کردووە.

2307
02:39:04.400 --> 02:39:06.160
<b>گەورەم، لە کوێ دەزانیت؟</b>

2308
02:39:06.640 --> 02:39:08.000
<b>هێشتا تێنەگەیشتوویت؟</b>

2309
02:39:08.240 --> 02:39:10.680
ئەو هەموو کون و کەلەبەرێکی پڕکردەوە
و ناوی خۆی لە هەموو شوێنێک سڕییەوە.

2310
02:39:10.760 --> 02:39:12.400
<b>ئەو پیاوەی باست کرد بوونی هەیە.</b>

2311
02:39:12.640 --> 02:39:14.000
<b>بەڵام تەنها لە تۆمارەکاندا.</b>

2312
02:39:14.440 --> 02:39:17.800
تاکە کێشەی ئەو لە ئێستادا ئەوەیە
کە نەهێڵێت نێلای
ڕاستییەکە بدرکێنێت.

2313
02:39:18.160 --> 02:39:20.240
<b>ئەویش دەزانێت کات خێرا تێدەپەڕێت.</b>

2314
02:39:20.640 --> 02:39:23.520
ئەم پیاوە و نێلای زۆر گرنگن
بۆ ئێمە تا ئەم دۆسیەیە
دابخەین.

2315
02:39:24.560 --> 02:39:28.160
دەبێت دڵنیابین کە شتەکان نەگەنە لوتکە
و کەس نەبێت
زیانی پێ بگەیەنێت.

2316
02:39:28.520 --> 02:39:30.240
<b>تەنها وەک ئەوەی پێم گوتيت قسەی لەگەڵ بکە.</b>

2317
02:39:31.240 --> 02:39:32.680
<b>تۆ زۆر باش دەیناسیت.</b>

2318
02:39:34.040 --> 02:39:36.000
دەتوانین تەنها بە تۆ
لە تەڵەی بخەین.

2319
02:39:38.000 --> 02:39:41.240
ئگەر یارمەتیمان بدەیت،
بێزاری ناکەین.

2320
02:39:41.400 --> 02:39:43.280
ئەویش ژیوانی نەبێت
کە تۆ بێزار بکات.

2321
02:39:43.400 --> 02:39:45.120
<b>ئەمە تەنها هەڵبژاردەی تۆیە.</b>

2322
02:39:46.280 --> 02:39:48.440
<b>ئەو ئێمە دەباتە لای پیاوە مەیموونەکە.</b>

2323
02:39:52.040 --> 02:39:53.240
<b>یارمەتیت دەدەم، گەورەم.</b>

2324
02:39:57.880 --> 02:40:00.040
تەنها ئەوە بکە کە دەیڵێم. بێگومان
دەکەوێتە داوەکەوە.

2325
02:40:02.920 --> 02:40:05.400
بەڵام بە من بەڵێن بدە کە هیچ زیانێک
بە من یان خێزانەکەم نەگات.

2326
02:40:07.640 --> 02:40:09.920
<b>I'll kill both of them together.</b>

2327
02:40:31.800 --> 02:40:37.120
Circulate this photo to all police stations,
railway
stations, toll gates, bus stands etc.

2328
02:40:37.440 --> 02:40:39.440
<b>Mainly West Kolkata...</b>

2329
02:40:40.240 --> 02:40:43.920
tell them to conduct a thorough search
around the tram
godown area.

2330
02:40:46.920 --> 02:40:49.560
<b>What if he doesn't step out?</b>

2331
02:40:53.040 --> 02:40:54.400
<b>He shouldn't step out.</b>

2332
02:40:54.640 --> 02:40:57.400
Even if he does, he should return
because he can't go
anywhere.

2333
02:40:58.520 --> 02:41:00.560
Because we can trap him
only inside his own place.

2334
02:41:06.000 --> 02:41:07.120
<b>I don't get it.</b>

2335
02:41:07.560 --> 02:41:10.520
I'm saying it is very easy to find out
where he's been
hiding all these days.

2336
02:41:10.560 --> 02:41:11.520
<b>How is that?</b>

2337
02:41:11.920 --> 02:41:14.000
<b>By his power and internet consumption.</b>

2338
02:41:14.560 --> 02:41:17.400
Hacking into Russia's Defence headquarters
is no ordinary
feat.

2339
02:41:18.120 --> 02:41:20.400
It requires a lot of data centres
and servers.

2340
02:41:20.760 --> 02:41:24.560
<b>It uses a lot of electricity and data.</b>

2341
02:41:24.760 --> 02:41:29.560
The Russian hack happened on Dec 27th,
at exactly 7:40 in
the evening.

2342
02:41:29.800 --> 02:41:32.240
<b>The time in India was 10:10 pm.</b>

2343
02:41:33.000 --> 02:41:41.000
If we make a list of the top 200 locations that
consumed
maximum power and internet during that date and
time...

2344
02:41:42.400 --> 02:41:44.400
<b>finding his location will be...</b>

2345
02:41:44.760 --> 02:41:45.800
<b>really easy.</b>

2346
02:41:45.880 --> 02:41:47.040
<b>You can go.</b>

2347
02:41:48.120 --> 02:41:49.280
<b>It's him!</b>

2348
02:41:49.640 --> 02:41:51.240
Catch him.
Hurry up!

2349
02:42:17.120 --> 02:42:19.880
Sir, there are 29 locations
that are common across these two
 lists.

2350
02:42:20.120 --> 02:42:22.680
Out of which 28 are IT parks,
and the other one is a mall.

2351
02:42:22.880 --> 02:42:23.920
<b>A mall?</b>

2352
02:42:24.400 --> 02:42:26.000
Which mall?
- Howrah Grand Mall.

2353
02:42:26.680 --> 02:42:28.120
<b>Howrah Grand Mall?</b>

2354
02:42:28.760 --> 02:42:31.000
But hasn't it been under renovation
for the last 1.5 years?

2355
02:42:31.040 --> 02:42:34.000
Moreover, they don't have permission
to do renovation work
during the nights.

2356
02:42:34.120 --> 02:42:36.560
Did you check properly?
- We did a thorough check, sir.

2357
02:42:36.640 --> 02:42:37.880
<b>Which area is the mall in?</b>

2358
02:43:11.640 --> 02:43:14.400
<b>Sir, I think we need backup.</b>

2359
02:43:14.640 --> 02:43:17.400
We should call for our forces
and bring this area under our
control.

2360
02:43:17.880 --> 02:43:19.920
They have already brought
this area under control, sir.

2361
02:43:20.000 --> 02:43:21.760
<b>What are you saying?</b>

2362
02:43:22.440 --> 02:43:24.800
Didn't you notice the
fresh tyre marks outside, sir?

2363
02:43:25.120 --> 02:43:28.000
Based on the turning radius,
I'd say 1 sedan, 3 SUVs, and 2
trucks.

2364
02:43:28.040 --> 02:43:30.440
Some 20-25 men have already
got here before us, sir.

2365
02:43:31.880 --> 02:43:34.240
You think they wouldn't have
brought the area under control,
 sir?

2366
02:43:34.400 --> 02:43:37.280
<b>Wow, wow, wow!</b>

2367
02:43:39.400 --> 02:43:42.000
Didn't I tell you
our guy is really talented?

2368
02:43:46.240 --> 02:43:47.920
<b>Who are you guys?</b>

2369
02:43:48.000 --> 02:43:50.560
You are pointing the gun
at the wrong guy, officer.

2370
02:43:51.640 --> 02:43:55.040
Two more seconds and I'm going to get
seriously offended.

2371
02:43:55.120 --> 02:43:57.640
Sir, call for backup.
- Drop the gun, Mr. Vishnu.

2372
02:43:57.760 --> 02:43:59.640
<b>Sir, call for backup.</b>

2373
02:43:59.760 --> 02:44:01.520
<b>Please drop your gun, Vishnu!</b>

2374
02:44:02.120 --> 02:44:03.120
<b>Sir...</b>

2375
02:44:11.000 --> 02:44:12.520
<b>Kathirvelan!</b>

2376
02:44:13.640 --> 02:44:15.400
<b>My best weapon.</b>

2377
02:44:17.120 --> 02:44:19.400
<b>I should actually be thanking you.</b>

2378
02:44:19.520 --> 02:44:21.400
<b>But thanks to what you did...</b>

2379
02:44:22.000 --> 02:44:24.640
you've put me in a situation
where I have to kill both of
you.

2380
02:44:26.880 --> 02:44:28.680
<b>All I can say now is...</b>

2381
02:44:30.640 --> 02:44:31.680
<b>sorry.</b>

2382
02:44:32.000 --> 02:44:32.880
<b>Sir...</b>

2383
02:44:33.440 --> 02:44:35.640
you don't have to say
sorry to me!

2384
02:44:36.240 --> 02:44:37.560
<b>You won't kill me, sir.</b>

2385
02:44:38.520 --> 02:44:39.760
<b>You can't kill me.</b>

2386
02:44:41.120 --> 02:44:42.120
<b>Oh, yeah?</b>

2387
02:44:42.160 --> 02:44:43.400
<b>Yes, sir.</b>

2388
02:44:43.880 --> 02:44:45.400
<b>I feel like...</b>

2389
02:44:45.640 --> 02:44:47.920
I might end up
harming you.

2390
02:44:50.640 --> 02:44:51.680
<b>Anand...</b>

2391
02:44:52.000 --> 02:44:53.120
<b>relax!</b>

2392
02:44:53.400 --> 02:44:54.400
<b>Anand...</b>

2393
02:44:54.520 --> 02:44:55.760
<b>relax!</b>

2394
02:44:55.880 --> 02:44:57.880
Sir, do you know what
an angel number is?

2395
02:44:57.920 --> 02:44:59.520
<b>1111, 2222...</b>

2396
02:44:59.640 --> 02:45:02.880
When we see such numbers,
anything we wish for will come
true.

2397
02:45:03.520 --> 02:45:05.520
<b>You've done a lot for me, sir.</b>

2398
02:45:05.880 --> 02:45:08.280
<b>Make one final wish, sir.</b>

2399
02:45:08.640 --> 02:45:13.520
In exactly 1-1-1-1-,
that is 11 minutes and 11 seconds...

2400
02:45:14.040 --> 02:45:15.280
<b>you...</b>

2401
02:45:16.040 --> 02:45:17.760
<b>and all these guys too...</b>

2402
02:45:17.920 --> 02:45:19.000
<b>will be killed by me!</b>

2403
02:45:19.040 --> 02:45:20.800
Do you have any idea
what you are saying?

2404
02:45:23.560 --> 02:45:25.000
<b>Do you get it, sir?</b>

2405
02:45:26.000 --> 02:45:27.240
<b>I do, sir.</b>

2406
02:45:27.640 --> 02:45:28.800
<b>This is fun.</b>

2407
02:45:29.520 --> 02:45:33.000
<b>So, 1-1-1-1.</b>

2408
02:45:33.880 --> 02:45:35.440
<b>11 minutes and 11 seconds?</b>

2409
02:45:37.880 --> 02:45:39.400
<b>Let's play this game.</b>

2410
02:45:40.000 --> 02:45:42.120
Let's see who wins.
You or me?

2411
02:45:53.120 --> 02:45:56.000
<b>You are making a big mistake, officer.</b>

2412
02:45:57.240 --> 02:46:00.440
He is a prime suspect, goddamn it.
Just tell me where the
hell he is.

2413
02:46:00.680 --> 02:46:03.520
Seriously? Fine, I will be
waiting right here.

2414
02:46:03.520 --> 02:46:06.120
If you don't hand him over to me
within the next two
hours...

2415
02:46:06.120 --> 02:46:08.400
I promise you there will be
severe consequences.

2416
02:46:42.520 --> 02:46:43.520
<b>Aslan...</b>

2417
02:46:44.160 --> 02:46:46.120
it was me who gave you 
those tipoffs all along.

2418
02:46:46.160 --> 02:46:48.120
I don't know if I'd still be alive
in some time.

2419
02:46:48.120 --> 02:46:52.160
The only way you can close your case
is with Nellai's
statement.

2420
02:46:52.680 --> 02:46:55.520
He will start blurting everything out
in exactly 30 minutes.

2421
02:46:55.560 --> 02:46:58.000
Kathir, Rishi, and all his men
are right here.

2422
02:46:59.120 --> 02:47:01.000
<b>Get here as fast as you can.</b>

2423
02:47:01.120 --> 02:47:02.520
<b>I've shared the location.</b>

2424
02:47:02.560 --> 02:47:05.000
<b>This is my last favour to you.</b>

2425
02:47:05.240 --> 02:47:06.440
<b>Don't spare him.</b>

2426
02:48:59.240 --> 02:49:00.440
<b>Mathi...</b>

2427
02:49:10.000 --> 02:49:12.400
Did we catch both the rats
in a single trap?

2428
02:49:12.520 --> 02:49:13.520
<b>Mathi...</b>

2429
02:49:13.880 --> 02:49:17.000
<b>What are you guys doing in there?</b>

2430
02:49:19.400 --> 02:49:20.440
<b>Come out!</b>

2431
02:49:24.120 --> 02:49:25.240
<b>Come at me!</b>

2432
02:49:43.560 --> 02:49:45.000
<b>Come on, guys!</b>

2433
02:49:48.440 --> 02:49:50.160
<b>You've only got three more minutes.</b>

2434
02:49:52.440 --> 02:49:53.560
<b>Fine!</b>

2435
02:49:53.760 --> 02:49:54.800
<b>Okay...</b>

2436
02:49:54.880 --> 02:49:58.040
You've done a lot for me.
It's just three more minutes.

2437
02:49:59.240 --> 02:50:00.560
<b>I will wait here.</b>

2438
02:50:02.640 --> 02:50:03.760
<b>Did you hear that?</b>

2439
02:50:05.760 --> 02:50:06.880
<b>Heard that?</b>

2440
02:50:11.160 --> 02:50:12.440
<b>You are the reason for all of this!</b>

2441
02:50:17.000 --> 02:50:20.120
I am happy to die
at your hands.

2442
02:50:24.640 --> 02:50:25.560
<b>I swear...</b>

2443
02:50:25.760 --> 02:50:27.000
<b>I didn't kill her.</b>

2444
02:50:28.400 --> 02:50:29.440
<b>I swear...</b>

2445
02:50:30.040 --> 02:50:32.400
<b>I was the one who called Jennifer.</b>

2446
02:50:32.640 --> 02:50:34.040
<b>Hear me out.</b>

2447
02:50:35.760 --> 02:50:37.040
<b>The problem has become serious.</b>

2448
02:50:37.160 --> 02:50:39.520
Both of you need to
get out of here immediately.

2449
02:50:39.640 --> 02:50:43.120
I've made all the arrangements
for you to go to Bangladesh
safely.

2450
02:50:43.240 --> 02:50:45.280
No one will be able
to find you.

2451
02:50:46.000 --> 02:50:47.760
<b>He is furious with me.</b>

2452
02:50:47.760 --> 02:50:49.120
I don't even know
if he'd believe me.

2453
02:50:49.160 --> 02:50:50.880
<b>I just want him to be safe.</b>

2454
02:50:51.280 --> 02:50:52.680
<b>Nothing else.</b>

2455
02:50:55.120 --> 02:50:56.640
<b>I hope no one saw you.</b>

2456
02:50:56.760 --> 02:50:58.520
<b>I just told my little sister.</b>

2457
02:50:58.560 --> 02:51:00.880
I don't even know if I'd ever
see her again.

2458
02:51:00.920 --> 02:51:03.000
<b>She has no one but for me.</b>

2459
02:51:04.640 --> 02:51:05.880
<b>Mathi!</b>

2460
02:51:06.000 --> 02:51:07.160
<b>Mathi...</b>

2461
02:51:15.680 --> 02:51:16.680
<b>Jenny...</b>

2462
02:51:21.400 --> 02:51:23.240
<b>Why are you crying now?</b>

2463
02:51:23.440 --> 02:51:26.040
Rather than being alive
and tarnishing our family honour...

2464
02:51:26.120 --> 02:51:27.240
<b>I am glad she died.</b>

2465
02:51:27.240 --> 02:51:29.520
Report this as an accident
and close the case!

2466
02:51:29.640 --> 02:51:32.760
And throw this mongrel's corpse
with other filth into the
sea.

2467
02:51:33.680 --> 02:51:36.920
I couldn't do anything
so I was...

2468
02:51:37.880 --> 02:51:39.920
<b>filled with anger and rage.</b>

2469
02:51:40.440 --> 02:51:42.760
<b>The people who killed you were...</b>

2470
02:51:44.880 --> 02:51:46.160
<b>happy...</b>

2471
02:51:47.520 --> 02:51:49.000
<b>I couldn't take it, little one.</b>

2472
02:51:50.240 --> 02:51:51.640
<b>I didn't spare any of them.</b>

2473
02:51:51.880 --> 02:51:53.120
<b>Not a single one.</b>

2474
02:51:54.160 --> 02:51:57.760
To my heart's content,
I went after them.

2475
02:52:03.000 --> 02:52:05.400
<b>Ever since I heard what happened to you...</b>

2476
02:52:11.120 --> 02:52:15.280
There is a beautiful life
waiting for you out there.

2477
02:52:16.760 --> 02:52:17.800
<b>Mathi...</b>

2478
02:52:19.640 --> 02:52:22.160
is a good teacher.
Everyone likes him.

2479
02:52:22.760 --> 02:52:25.880
Remember what Ma told us?
It's such a good life.

2480
02:52:27.760 --> 02:52:29.400
<b>What are you saying, Kathir?</b>

2481
02:52:29.640 --> 02:52:31.240
<b>It's called game theory, man.</b>

2482
02:52:31.760 --> 02:52:35.120
A mathematician knows how to
get away with minimal loss.

2483
02:52:35.240 --> 02:52:37.280
<b>That is...</b>

2484
02:52:37.640 --> 02:52:40.680
instead of losing two lives,
you are trying to save atleast
one...

2485
02:52:40.760 --> 02:52:41.880
<b>so you are taking revenge!</b>

2486
02:52:41.920 --> 02:52:44.120
That's superb.
First class!

2487
02:52:55.520 --> 02:52:56.520
<b>Sorry.</b>

2488
02:53:03.040 --> 02:53:04.000
<b>Kathir...</b>

2489
02:53:07.400 --> 02:53:08.640
<b>Who were you--</b>

2490
02:53:09.640 --> 02:53:10.640
<b>Oh...</b>

2491
02:53:11.440 --> 02:53:13.000
<b>You don't know that, do you?</b>

2492
02:53:14.520 --> 02:53:16.120
<b>Even as a kid, I had headaches.</b>

2493
02:53:16.680 --> 02:53:18.920
It felt like a machine was running
inside my head.

2494
02:53:19.400 --> 02:53:20.440
<b>It hurt so bad.</b>

2495
02:53:21.120 --> 02:53:22.640
<b>These people used to come to me.</b>

2496
02:53:23.640 --> 02:53:24.800
<b>And offer me a lot of advice.</b>

2497
02:53:26.440 --> 02:53:27.680
<b>You used to come, too.</b>

2498
02:53:28.760 --> 02:53:31.000
You used to smile
when you talked to me.

2499
02:53:31.400 --> 02:53:33.160
<b>This is called a hallucination.</b>

2500
02:53:33.760 --> 02:53:35.880
They say it can be cured
with treatment.

2501
02:53:37.120 --> 02:53:38.880
This was the only way
I could talk to you.

2502
02:53:39.000 --> 02:53:40.400
<b>But without it...</b>

2503
02:53:41.120 --> 02:53:42.440
<b>how would I survive?</b>

2504
02:53:44.560 --> 02:53:46.000
<b>So I didn't undergo treatment.</b>

2505
02:53:50.760 --> 02:53:52.680
<b>Time's up!</b>

2506
02:53:55.560 --> 02:53:58.760
Please wait. Aslan will be here shortly,
he will take care
of everything.

2507
02:53:59.000 --> 02:54:00.000
<b>Kathir, don't...</b>

2508
02:54:00.160 --> 02:54:03.120
If you step out of the door,
you won't survive.

2509
02:54:04.120 --> 02:54:05.400
<b>If something happens to you...</b>

2510
02:54:05.680 --> 02:54:07.760
I can't get away with the crimes
I've committed.

2511
02:54:09.440 --> 02:54:11.880
Rishi will never let us live
as long as he is around.

2512
02:54:12.880 --> 02:54:14.760
<b>One person should take all the blame.</b>

2513
02:54:15.400 --> 02:54:16.680
<b>You are Mathi now.</b>

2514
02:54:18.920 --> 02:54:20.120
<b>Continue being Mathi.</b>

2515
02:55:06.120 --> 02:55:07.440
<b>Shoot him!</b>

2516
02:55:08.680 --> 02:55:09.880
<b>Shoot him!</b>

2517
02:55:11.640 --> 02:55:13.440
Attaboy!
Let's leave.

2518
02:55:23.440 --> 02:55:24.560
<b>Shoot him!</b>

2519
02:55:30.760 --> 02:55:32.000
<b>Shoot him!</b>

2520
02:55:34.520 --> 02:55:35.640
<b>Come on!</b>

2521
02:55:36.800 --> 02:55:38.400
<b>Shoot him!</b>

2522
02:56:03.920 --> 02:56:05.920
<b>Shoot him!</b>

2523
02:56:42.400 --> 02:56:43.880
<b>Shoot him!</b>

2524
02:56:47.400 --> 02:56:48.560
<b>Yeah!</b>

2525
02:57:57.400 --> 02:57:58.640
<b>My little brother...</b>

2526
02:57:59.240 --> 02:58:00.400
<b>poor guy.</b>

2527
02:58:01.280 --> 02:58:02.520
<b>It was me...</b>

2528
02:58:06.280 --> 02:58:07.520
<b>but he...</b>

2529
02:58:11.920 --> 02:58:14.640
<b>Nothing should happen to him.</b>

2530
02:58:15.880 --> 02:58:19.160
<b>I don't care what happens to me.</b>

2531
02:58:19.680 --> 02:58:23.000
<b>Look what I've done to his life...</b>

2532
02:58:24.120 --> 02:58:25.160
<b>He...</b>

2533
02:58:26.800 --> 02:58:28.000
<b>He should live.</b>

2534
02:58:35.760 --> 02:58:36.800
<b>Sorry.</b>

2535
02:58:58.400 --> 02:58:59.880
<b>Thank you, Mathi.</b>

2536
02:59:06.000 --> 02:59:07.440
<b>I might be Mathi.</b>

2537
02:59:09.280 --> 02:59:11.120
<b>When everyone calls me now...</b>

2538
02:59:12.120 --> 02:59:15.280
I might hear the name 'Mathi'
millions of times.

2539
02:59:18.000 --> 02:59:21.880
But the only name that will be
running in my mind is...

2540
02:59:22.880 --> 02:59:23.880
<b>Kathir.</b>

2541
02:59:25.240 --> 02:59:26.240
<b>Kathir!</b>

2542
02:59:29.120 --> 02:59:30.120
<b>Kathir...</b>

2543
02:59:32.920 --> 02:59:36.160
Kathir, no matter where you are,
I know you are watching
over me.

2544
02:59:37.400 --> 02:59:40.400
I know if I am in trouble,
you will be there for me.

2545
02:59:41.680 --> 02:59:43.920
<b>I know you'd do anything for me.</b>

2546
02:59:46.120 --> 02:59:48.880
<b>Can you do one last thing for me?</b>

2547
02:59:51.040 --> 02:59:53.040
<b>If there is a next life...</b>

2548
02:59:53.800 --> 02:59:57.240
<b>will you be my sibling again, Kathir?</b>

2549
02:59:59.120 --> 03:00:00.120
<b>Please?</b>
